{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012KsasfbbSX885Ui5wSbr1T","type":"tool_result","content":"16707 session.js.dl\n27469 harness.html.dl\n13624 bridge.js.dl\n20248 round.js.dl\n17587 README.md.dl\n6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a  session.js.dl\ntotal 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:56 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 6 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:56 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 13624 Nov  5 01:56 bridge.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 27469 Nov  5 01:56 harness.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 17587 Nov  5 01:56 hub-readme.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 20248 Nov  5 01:56 round.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16707 Nov  5 01:56 session-client.txt\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\" />\n    <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\" />\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../engine/ui/touch.css\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>The starter game: my-3dge</title>\n    <!--\n      The starter game's page (labs/game/README.md): labs/game/main.ts starts the engine on the scene game:play and\n      shows the round in the HUD. Ready or error: until the engine publishes window.__engine, the inline script below\n      records a script that fails to load or throws, and shows it in #msg, so a broken page is one line of text,\n      never a blank one; `node x shot labs/game` reports the same headless.\n    -->\n    <style>\n      html,\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        height: 100%;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        background: #15171c;\n      }\n      canvas {\n        display: block;\n        width: 100vw;\n        height: 100vh;\n        height: 100dvh;\n        outline: none;\n        touch-action: none;\n      }\n      #msg {\n        position: fixed;\n        inset: 0;\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        padding: 24px;\n        font:\n          18px system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        color: #c9ccd4;\n        text-align: center;\n        white-space: pre-line;\n        pointer-events: none;\n      }\n      #msg[hidden] {\n        display: none;\n      }\n    </style>\n    <script>\n      window.__engine = { ready: false, errors: [] };\n      function gameFailed(message) {\n        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return; // the engine reports now\n        var fix = 'the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless';\n        var record = { code: 'APP_START', message: 'the page failed to start: ' + message, fix: fix };\n        if (window.__engine.errors.length === 0) {\n          var msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n          if (msg) msg.textContent = record.code + ': ' + record.message + '\\nFix: ' + fix;\n        }\n        window.__engine.errors.push(record);\n      }\n      addEventListener('error', function (event) {\n        gameFailed(event.message || 'a script failed');\n      });\n      addEventListener('unhandledrejection', function (event) {\n        gameFailed(String((event.reason && event.reason.message) || event.reason));\n      });\n    </script>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas>\n    <div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading…</div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./main.ts\" onerror=\"gameFailed('labs/game/main.ts did not load')\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n# The starter game\n\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\n\n## The game\n\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\n\n## Files\n\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\n\n## Settings\n\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\n\n## See it\n\n```sh\n/**\n * @file Vite's settings (the dev server and the build) and Vitest's (T1), in one file as Vitest expects (PLAN.md\n * §6.10, WPs 0.2 and 0.12).\n *\n * Invariants: every lab page (`labs/<name>/index.html`) and test page (`tests/pages/<name>.html`) is served as its\n * own page, and a missing page is a 404 (`appType: 'mpa'`). A bare `three` resolves to `three/webgpu`, as three.js's\n * WebGPU examples map it. The runtime dependencies are pre-bundled at startup, so a first page load never\n * re-optimizes and reloads (§4.7). The server listens on 127.0.0.1 and `$PORT` (default 5173). Every test file runs\n * the advice trap first (tests/setup/adviceTrap.ts), and `vitest --changed` reruns everything on the files that\n * tools/lib/tiers.ts's `T1_FULL` names.\n *\n * The build (`npm run build`) writes dist/ from the landing page (the root's\n * `index.html`) and every `labs/<name>/index.html`; test pages never ship (`harness.html` throws on purpose). In a game\n * made from the engine (engine-lock.json at its root, ADR-0024) the box is the worked example: served, never built. A page\n * ships only what it imports, never a `fetch()` of a repository path (§6.3). Nothing here needs the network, a\n * browser, the source checkouts or an `x` command: the build and Vitest both read this file. The one-file\n * playground (playground.html, tools/lib/oneFile.ts) is built apart, with this file's alias. The reference to\n * `vitest/config`, which adds `test` to Vite's config type, is kept in the declaration tsc -b emits (`preserve`), so\n * the tests' project, which sees this file through it, knows `config.test` (Vitest 4's main types no longer add it).\n *\n * @see tools/lib/vite.test.ts\n */\n/// <reference types=\"vitest/config\" preserve=\"true\" />\nimport { existsSync, globSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { availableParallelism } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport { vitestRerunTriggers } from './tools/lib/tiers';\n\n/** The dev server's port: `$PORT` (each ultracode lane sets its own), else 5173. */\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT) || 5173;\n\n/** The repository root: this file's directory. */\nconst ROOT = import.meta.dirname;\n\n/** Whether this is a game made from the engine (tools/game/new-game.mjs), not the engine's own repository. */\nconst GAME = existsSync(join(ROOT, 'engine-lock.json'));\n\n/** The pages a build ships, as absolute paths by entry name: `index` (the landing page), then `labs/<name>`. */\nconst PAGES = Object.fromEntries(\n  ['index.html', ...globSync('labs/*/index.html', { cwd: ROOT }).sort()]\n    .filter((page) => !(GAME && page.startsWith('labs/box/')))\n    .map((page) => [dirname(page) === '.' ? 'index' : dirname(page), join(ROOT, page)]),\n);\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  appType: 'mpa',\n  resolve: {\n    alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }],\n  },\n  optimizeDeps: {\n    // The pages Vite scans for imports; the default (every *.html under the root) would crawl .cache/.\n    entries: ['index.html', 'labs/*/index.html', 'tests/pages/*.html'],\n    // Every runtime dependency of package.json, by the entry points pages import (tools/lib/vite.test.ts checks it).\n    include: [\n      'three/webgpu',\n      'three/tsl',\n      '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat',\n      '@stdlib/math-base-special-sin',\n      '@stdlib/math-base-special-cos',","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"f659b7e5-35b3-4314-85f8-346de2c32ac9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:56:54.296Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"16707 session.js.dl\n27469 harness.html.dl\n13624 bridge.js.dl\n20248 round.js.dl\n17587 README.md.dl\n6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a  session.js.dl\ntotal 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:56 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 6 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:56 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 13624 Nov  5 01:56 bridge.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 27469 Nov  5 01:56 harness.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 17587 Nov  5 01:56 hub-readme.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 20248 Nov  5 01:56 round.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16707 Nov  5 01:56 session-client.txt\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\" />\n    <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\" />\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../engine/ui/touch.css\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>The starter game: my-3dge</title>\n    <!--\n      The starter game's page (labs/game/README.md): labs/