round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\n\n## See it\n\n```sh\n/**\n * @file Vite's settings (the dev server and the build) and Vitest's (T1), in one file as Vitest expects (PLAN.md\n * §6.10, WPs 0.2 and 0.12).\n *\n * Invariants: every lab page (`labs/<name>/index.html`) and test page (`tests/pages/<name>.html`) is served as its\n * own page, and a missing page is a 404 (`appType: 'mpa'`). A bare `three` resolves to `three/webgpu`, as three.js's\n * WebGPU examples map it. The runtime dependencies are pre-bundled at startup, so a first page load never\n * re-optimizes and reloads (§4.7). The server listens on 127.0.0.1 and `$PORT` (default 5173). Every test file runs\n * the advice trap first (tests/setup/adviceTrap.ts), and `vitest --changed` reruns everything on the files that\n * tools/lib/tiers.ts's `T1_FULL` names.\n *\n * The build (`npm run build`) writes dist/ from the landing page (the root's\n * `index.html`) and every `labs/<name>/index.html`; test pages never ship (`harness.html` throws on purpose). In a game\n * made from the engine (engine-lock.json at its root, ADR-0024) the box is the worked example: served, never built. A page\n * ships only what it imports, never a `fetch()` of a repository path (§6.3). Nothing here needs the network, a\n * browser, the source checkouts or an `x` command: the build and Vitest both read this file. The one-file\n * playground (playground.html, tools/lib/oneFile.ts) is built apart, with this file's alias. The reference to\n * `vitest/config`, which adds `test` to Vite's config type, is kept in the declaration tsc -b emits (`preserve`), so\n * the tests' project, which sees this file through it, knows `config.test` (Vitest 4's main types no longer add it).\n *\n * @see tools/lib/vite.test.ts\n */\n/// <reference types=\"vitest/config\" preserve=\"true\" />\nimport { existsSync, globSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { availableParallelism } from 'node:os';\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport { vitestRerunTriggers } from './tools/lib/tiers';\n\n/** The dev server's port: `$PORT` (each ultracode lane sets its own), else 5173. */\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT) || 5173;\n\n/** The repository root: this file's directory. */\nconst ROOT = import.meta.dirname;\n\n/** Whether this is a game made from the engine (tools/game/new-game.mjs), not the engine's own repository. */\nconst GAME = existsSync(join(ROOT, 'engine-lock.json'));\n\n/** The pages a build ships, as absolute paths by entry name: `index` (the landing page), then `labs/<name>`. */\nconst PAGES = Object.fromEntries(\n  ['index.html', ...globSync('labs/*/index.html', { cwd: ROOT }).sort()]\n    .filter((page) => !(GAME && page.startsWith('labs/box/')))\n    .map((page) => [dirname(page) === '.' ? 'index' : dirname(page), join(ROOT, page)]),\n);\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  appType: 'mpa',\n  resolve: {\n    alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }],\n  },\n  optimizeDeps: {\n    // The pages Vite scans for imports; the default (every *.html under the root) would crawl .cache/.\n    entries: ['index.html', 'labs/*/index.html', 'tests/pages/*.html'],\n    // Every runtime dependency of package.json, by the entry points pages import (tools/lib/vite.test.ts checks it).\n    include: [\n      'three/webgpu',\n      'three/tsl',\n      '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat',\n      '@stdlib/math-base-special-sin',\n      '@stdlib/math-base-special-cos',","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012KsasfbbSX885Ui5wSbr1T","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
