{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01639uErW9Bu11dm3if4Kw2r","type":"tool_result","content":"   Start at  01:57:14\n   Duration  11.23s (transform 10.55s, setup 108ms, import 14.89s, tests 3.51s, environment 0ms)\n\nJSON report written to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601/out/test/report.json\nchromium-1243\nchromium_headless_shell-1243\nffmpeg-1011\nfirefox-1543\nwebkit-2359\n# Templates\n\n`node x new <kind> <id>` writes a working entry of a kind from its template here: the module and its unit test,\nformatted, then its checks (types, lint, its test, docs) and the step that comes next. It never overwrites a file.\n`node x new` lists the kinds with what each id looks like; `node x new <kind> --test` writes a kind's sample, checks\nit and removes it, and `node x new --test-all` tests every kind (the full run, `node x ci --local --full`, runs it),\nso no template rots. tools/cmd/new.ts's file comment is the manual (the manifest's keys, the placeholders, the\nchecks); the `add-entry` skill (.claude/skills/add-entry/SKILL.md) is the loop round it.\n\n## The kinds\n\nEach row is a directory here; tools/cmd/new.test.ts fails a kind this table leaves out, or a path its kind refuses.\n\"Seen with\" names a command that shows or checks an entry beyond its own test; `x new` prints the rest of what to do\nafter writing one (its manifest's `next`). A kind marked \"no\" in \"In a game\" makes no entry there and says what a\ngame does instead (its manifest's `games`).\n\n| Kind           | An entry is                                                    | Its path                               | Seen with                                         | In a game |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| `action`       | a multi-beat sequence a body plays (`defineAction`)            | `labs/<lab>/actions/<name>`            | its test (`actionCheck` through `animCheckBody`)  | yes       |\n| `body`         | a puppet body on the humanoid's bones (`defineBody`)           | `labs/<lab>/bodies/<name>`             | `node x gallery body body:<name>`                 | yes       |\n| `build`        | the humanoid's proportions (`defineBuild`)                     | `labs/<lab>/builds/<name>`             | its test (`animCheck` of its rest pose)           | yes       |\n| `camera`       | a camera mode of a game's own, `cam3=<name>` (`defineCamera`)  | `labs/<lab>/cameras/<name>`            | `node x shot <page> --cam cam3=<name>`            | yes       |\n| `course`       | a playground feel course (`defineCourse`)                      | `labs/playground/courses/<name>`       | `node x feel labs/playground --course <name>`     | no        |\n| `emitter`      | a particle effect as data (`defineEmitter`)                    | `labs/<lab>/emitters/<name>`           | `node x gallery emitter emitter:<name>`           | yes       |\n| `feature`      | a rendering technique behind its feature and advice            | `engine/gfx/enhanced/<name>`           | `node x perf <lab> --feature feature:<name>`      | no        |\n| `geometry`     | a shape built from the kit's builders (`defineGeometry`)       | `labs/<lab>/geometry/<name>`           | `node x qa geo --only geometry:<name>`            | yes       |\n| `interactable` | what a player uses and strikes (`defineUsable`, `defineStrikable`) | `labs/<lab>/interactables/<name>`  | its test (a player's use and punch in a yard)     | yes       |\n| `level`        | a level written as storeys (`defineLevel`)                     | `labs/<lab>/levels/<name>`             | `node x eye <scene>` (a scene that plays it)      | yes       |\n| `look`         | a material style and a filter chain (`defineLook`)             | `labs/<lab>/looks/<name>`              | `node x gallery look look:<name>`                 | yes       |\n| `material`     | three.js's classic parameters as data (`defineMaterial`)       | `labs/<lab>/materials/<name>`          | `node x gallery material material:<name>`         | yes       |\n| `module`       | a TypeScript module and its unit test                          | `<engine\\|tools\\|labs\\|tests>/<dir>/<name>` | `npm test -- <path>`                         | yes       |\n| `move`         | a named strike in metres and seconds (`defineMove`)            | `labs/<lab>/moves/<name>`              | `node x gallery move move:<name>`                 | yes       |\n| `movement`     | how a character moves (`defineMovement`)                       | `labs/<lab>/movement/<name>`           | `node x sim <scene> --feel`                       | yes       |\n| `prop`         | a thing that stands in a level (`defineProp`)                  | `labs/<lab>/props/<name>`              | `node x gallery prop prop:<name>`, `node x qa geo tex --only prop:<name>` | yes |\n| `rig`          | a procedural creature of engine/anim/proc's blocks              | `labs/<lab>/rigs/<name>`               | its test (`rigCheck`, and a walk)                 | yes       |\n| `scene`        | a box scene and its replay test (`defineScene`)                | `labs/box/scenes/<name>`               | `node x sim`, `node x replay`, `node x shot labs/box --scene <name>` | no |\n| `sfx`          | a sound effect for the DSP core (`defineSfx`)                  | `labs/<lab>/sounds/<name>`             | `node x audio sfx:<name>`                         | yes       |\n| `song`         | a tune in tracker notation (`defineSong`)                      | `labs/<lab>/sounds/<name>`             | `node x audio song:<name>`                        | yes       |\n| `telegraph`    | an attack's warning shape on the floor (`defineTelegraph`)     | `labs/<lab>/telegraphs/<name>`         | its test (a hit inside, a near miss past it)      | yes       |\n| `texture`      | a seeded, periodic texture generator (`defineTexture`)         | `labs/<lab>/textures/<name>`           | `node x qa tex --only texture:<name>`             | yes       |\n| `thing`        | what can be hit, as data (`defineThing`)                       | `labs/<lab>/things/<name>`             | its test (struck down, standing again)            | yes       |\n| `weapon`       | a firearm and the prop it is drawn as (`defineWeapon`)         | `labs/<lab>/weapons/<name>`            | `node x gallery prop prop:<name>`                 | yes       |\n\n`<lab>` is the lab that shows it (`box`, `playground`…; `game` in a game). The gallery (`node x gallery`, PLAN.md WP\n7.7) films what its page registers: its page (tests/pages/gallery.ts) imports every lab's `scenes/`, `looks/` and\n`bodies/`, so an emitter, a prop or a weapon is filmed once a scene imports its module (`--page` films a lab's own\npage instead).\n\n## Adding a kind\n\nA kind gets its template when an agent writes the third entry of it by hand (PLAN.md §8.13); the work package that\nwrites that entry adds the template, and its row here.\n\n1. `tools/templates/<kind>/`: `template.json` and the template files. Its keys: `describe` (one sentence, which\n   `node x new` lists), `id` (what an id looks like, with an example), `pattern` (a regular expression every id\n   matches; let it take `tools/templates/<kind>/<name>`, where the sample is written), `sample`\n   (`tools/templates/<kind>/sample<Kind>`), `files` (template file → target: `{{id}}.ts`, `{{id}}.test.ts`), `checks`\n   (`types`, `lint`, `test`, `docs`), and when they help, `next` (what to do after writing one, which `x new` prints)\n   and `games` (for a kind a game makes none of, what it does instead).\n2. Write it from a real entry of the kind: the file comment's first sentence says \"replace this text\", and the rest\ntools/templates/action:\naction.test.ts.tmpl\naction.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/body:\nbody.test.ts.tmpl\nbody.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/build:\nbuild.test.ts.tmpl\nbuild.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/camera:\ncamera.test.ts.tmpl\ncamera.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/emitter:\nemitter.test.ts.tmpl\nemitter.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/look:\nlook.test.ts.tmpl\nlook.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/prop:\nprop.test.ts.tmpl\nprop.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/sfx:\nsfx.test.ts.tmpl\nsfx.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/song:\nsong.test.ts.tmpl\nsong.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n/**\n * @file The box's slime (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): a ball that hops after the hero, from Box 4 on. `SLIME` holds its\n * numbers, `CROWD_SLIME` its own component (`crowdSlime`: where it is in its hop and for how long, beside the crowd\n * agent the scene keeps), `makeSlime` draws one, and `steerSlime` moves it each step: on the floor it brakes, rests,\n * crouches and leaps; in the air it flies on until it lands.\n *\n * Its hop, the prototype's: after a rest it crouches for `SLIME.crouch`, then leaps (`hop`, engine/world/steer.ts)\n * `SLIME.reach` metres along the flow field toward the hero's tile, up at `SLIME.up` m/s, so it lands where it aimed\n * under its own gravity, onto a stair as well as across the floor; level with the hero it keeps to a ring round him\n * instead, leaping in from beyond it by what it lacks and out from inside it. A hop too short to bother with, or one\n * out of reach, waits a moment. After landing it rests for `SLIME.rest` plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`, drawn from the\n * crowd's stream.\n *\n * Its pounce (Box 5, WP 6.7): `SLIME_ATTACK`. Resting on its ring round the hero, cooled down and granted one of his\n * attack tokens, it squats for `wind` s, its line telegraph (`telegraph:boxPounce`) filling toward him, then leaps at\n * where he stood, up at `up` m/s, to land just short of him; touching him on the way takes `damage` hit points and\n * throws it back off him. Landed, it gives the token back and rests `rest` s plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`. A hit on\n * it breaks its pounce off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's slime (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:200-203, 387-414`), in SI units\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical): a ball of radius 6 units\n * → 0.375 m; leaps of 150 units/s up → 9.375 m/s (`HOP.up`), at most 44 units → 2.75 m (`HOP.reach`), after a crouch\n * of 0.28 s; a rest of 0.45 s plus up to 0.6 s; braking at 400 units/s² → 25 m/s²; its ring 34 units → 2.125 m, its\n * band 8 units → 0.5 m. Its first rest is drawn from its spawn, up to 1 s.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as a blob (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `SLIME.looks`, squashed by where it\n * is in its hop (`SLIME.squash`); the blob's spring makes the bounce.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * SLIME.reach; // 2.75: m, its longest hop\n * // steerSlime(physics, agent, slime, chase); // in the phase ai, each step\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  HOP,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineTelegraph,\n  followFlow,\n  hop,\n  knockback,\n  launch,\n  setVelocity,\n  Vector3,\n  type CrowdAgent,\n  type Physics,\n  type Rng,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { levelWith, type Chase } from './walker';\n\n/** The prototype's units per metre (PLAN.md Appendix C). */\nconst UNITS = 16;\n\n/** The slime's numbers (see the file comment). */\nexport const SLIME = Object.freeze({\n  /** Its body: a ball (m). */\n  agent: Object.freeze({ shape: 'ball', radius: 6 / UNITS } as const),\n  /** How fast it leaps up (m/s), and its longest leap (m). */\n  up: HOP.up,\n  reach: HOP.reach,\n  /** A leap shorter than this (m) is not worth it: it waits `SLIME.wait` instead. */\n  least: 4 / UNITS,\n  /** Seconds it crouches before a leap, waits after a leap it skipped, and rests after landing (plus a spread). */\n  crouch: 0.28,\n  wait: 0.3,\n  rest: 0.45,\n  restSpread: 0.6,\n  /** In the air at least this long (s) before it can land. */\n  airborne: 0.1,\n  /** How hard it brakes on the floor (m/s²). */\n  brake: 400 / UNITS,\n  /** The ring it keeps round the hero (m), and its band either side (m). */\n  ring: Object.freeze({ radius: 34 / UNITS, band: 8 / UNITS }),\n  /** Its looks, one drawn per slime: the prototype's `SLIME_PARTS`, plain twice, horns, cat ears, wings. */\n  looks: Object.freeze(['', '', 'horns', 'ears', 'wings']),\n  /** The squash its body eases to (engine/anim/blob.ts): flat in its crouch, stretched rising, braced falling. */\n  squash: Object.freeze({ rest: 0, crouch: -0.35, rising: 0.25, falling: -0.1 }),\n});","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"8131b8ee-79a5-464d-86ac-7b1f2fba35ee","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:57:26.020Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"   Start at  01:57:14\n   Duration  11.23s (transform 10.55s, setup 108ms, import 14.89s, tests 3.51s, environment 0ms)\n\nJSON report written to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601/out/test/report.json\nchromium-1243\nchromium_headless_shell-1243\nffmpeg-1011\nfirefox-1543\nwebkit-2359\n# Templates\n\n`node x new <kind> <id>` writes a working entry of a kind from its template here: the module and its unit test,\nformatted, then its checks (types, lint, its test, docs) and the step that comes next. It never overwrites a file.\n`node x new` lists the kinds with what each id looks like; `node x new <kind> --test` writes a kind's sample, checks\nit and removes it, and `node x new --test-all` tests every kind (the full run, `node x ci --local --full`, runs it),\nso no template rots. tools/cmd/new.ts's file comment is the manual (the manifest's keys, the placeholders, the\nchecks); the `add-entry` skill (.claude/skills/add-entry/SKILL.md) is the loop round it.\n\n## The kinds\n\nEach row is a directory here; tools/cmd/new.test.ts fails a kind this table leaves out, or a path its kind refuses.\n\"Seen with\" names a command that shows or checks an entry beyond its own test; `x new` prints the rest of what to do\nafter writing one (its manifest's `next`). A kind marked \"no\" in \"In a game\" makes no entry there and says what a\ngame does instead (its manifest's `games`).\n\n| Kind           | An entry is                                                    | Its path                               | Seen with                                         | In a game |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | --------- |\n| `action`       | a multi-beat sequence a body plays (`defineAction`)            | `labs/<lab>/actions/<name>`            | its test (`actionCheck` through `animCheckBody`)  | yes       |\n| `body`         | a puppet body on the humanoid's bones (`defineBody`)           | `labs/<lab>/bodies/<name>`             | `node x gallery body body:<name>`                 | yes       |\n| `build`        | the humanoid's proportions (`defineBuild`)                     | `labs/<lab>/builds/<name>`             | its test (`animCheck` of its rest pose)           | yes       |\n| `camera`       | a camera mode of a game's own, `cam3=<name>` (`defineCamera`)  | `labs/<lab>/cameras/<name>`            | `node x shot <page> --cam cam3=<name>`            | yes       |\n| `course`       | a playground feel course (`defineCourse`)                      | `labs/playground/courses/<name>`       | `node x feel labs/playground --course <name>`     | no        |\n| `emitter`      | a particle effect as data (`defineEmitter`)                    | `labs/<lab>/emitters/<name>`           | `node x gallery emitter emitter:<name>`           | yes       |\n| `feature`      | a rendering technique behind its feature and advice            | `engine/gfx/enhanced/<name>`           | `node x perf <lab> --feature feature:<name>`      | no        |\n| `geometry`     | a shape built from the kit's builders (`defineGeometry`)       | `labs/<lab>/geometry/<name>`           | `node x qa geo --only geometry:<name>`            | yes       |\n| `interactable` | what a player uses and strikes (`defineUsable`, `defineStrikable`) | `labs/<lab>/interactables/<name>`  | its test (a player's use and punch in a yard)     | yes       |\n| `level`        | a level written as storeys (`defineLevel`)                     | `labs/<lab>/levels/<name>`             | `node x eye <scene>` (a scene that plays it)      | yes       |\n| `look`         | a material style and a filter chain (`defineLook`)             | `labs/<lab>/looks/<name>`              | `node x gallery look look:<name>`                 | yes       |\n| `material`     | three.js's classic parameters as data (`defineMaterial`)       | `labs/<lab>/materials/<name>`          | `node x gallery material material:<name>`         | yes       |\n| `module`       | a TypeScript module and its unit test                          | `<engine\\|tools\\|labs\\|tests>/<dir>/<name>` | `npm test -- <path>`                         | yes       |\n| `move`         | a named strike in metres and seconds (`defineMove`)            | `labs/<lab>/moves/<name>`              | `node x gallery move move:<name>`                 | yes       |\n| `movement`     | how a character moves (`defineMovement`)                       | `labs/<lab>/movement/<name>`           | `node x sim <scene> --feel`                       | yes       |\n| `prop`         | a thing that stands in a level (`defineProp`)                  | `labs/<lab>/props/<name>`              | `node x gallery prop prop:<name>`, `node x qa geo tex --only prop:<name>` | yes |\n| `rig`          | a procedural creature of engine/anim/proc's blocks              | `labs/<lab>/rigs/<name>`               | its test (`rigCheck`, and a walk)                 | yes       |\n| `scene`        | a box scene and its replay test (`defineScene`)                | `labs/box/scenes/<name>`               | `node x sim`, `node x replay`, `node x shot labs/box --scene <name>` | no |\n| `sfx`          | a sound effect for the DSP core (`defineSfx`)                  | `labs/<lab>/sounds/<name>`             | `node x audio sfx:<name>`                         | yes       |\n| `song`         | a tune in tracker notation (`defineSong`)                      | `labs/<lab>/sounds/<name>`             | `node x audio song:<name>`                        | yes       |\n| `telegraph`    | an attack's warning shape on the floor (`defineTelegraph`)     | `labs/<lab>/telegraphs/<name>`         | its test (a hit inside, a near miss past it)      | yes       |\n| `texture`      | a seeded, periodic texture generator (`defineTexture`)         | `labs/<lab>/textures/<name>`           | `node x qa tex --only texture:<name>`             | yes       |\n| `thing`        | what can be hit, as data (`defineThing`)                       | `labs/<lab>/things/<name>`             | its test (struck down, standing again)            | yes       |\n| `weapon`       | a firearm and the prop it is drawn as (`defineWeapon`)         | `labs/<lab>/weapons/<name>`            | `node x gallery prop prop:<name>`                 | yes       |\n\n`<lab>` is the lab that shows it (`box`, `playground`…; `game` in a game). The gallery (`node x gallery`, PLAN.md WP\n7.7) films what its page registers: its page (tests/pages/gallery.ts) imports every lab's `scenes/`, `looks/` and\n`bodies/`, so an emitter, a prop or a weapon is filmed once a scene imports its module (`--page` films a lab's own\npage instead).\n\n## Adding a kind\n\nA kind gets its template when an agent writes the third entry of it by hand (PLAN.md §8.13); the work package that\nwrites that entry adds the template, and its row here.\n\n1. `tools/templates/<kind>/`: `template.json` and the template files. Its keys: `describe` (one sentence, which\n   `node x new` lists), `id` (what an id looks like, with an example), `pattern` (a regular expression every id\n   matches; let it take `tools/templates/<kind>/<name>`, where the sample is written), `sample`\n   (`tools/templates/<kind>/sample<Kind>`), `files` (template file → target: `{{id}}.ts`, `{{id}}.test.ts`), `checks`\n   (`types`, `lint`, `test`, `docs`), and when they help, `next` (what to do after writing one, which `x new` prints)\n   and `games` (for a kind a game makes none of, what it does instead).\n2. Write it from a real entry of the kind: the file comment's first sentence says \"replace this text\", and the rest\ntools/templates/action:\naction.test.ts.tmpl\naction.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/body:\nbody.test.ts.tmpl\nbody.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/build:\nbuild.test.ts.tmpl\nbuild.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/camera:\ncamera.test.ts.tmpl\ncamera.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/emitter:\nemitter.test.ts.tmpl\nemitter.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/look:\nlook.test.ts.tmpl\nlook.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/prop:\nprop.test.ts.tmpl\nprop.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/sfx:\nsfx.test.ts.tmpl\nsfx.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n\ntools/templates/song:\nsong.test.ts.tmpl\nsong.ts.tmpl\ntemplate.json\n/**\n * @file The box's slime (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): a ball that hops after the hero, from Box 4 on. `SLIME` holds its\n * numbers, `CROWD_SLIME` its own component (`crowdSlime`: where it is in its hop and for how long, beside the crowd\n * agent the scene keeps), `makeSlime` draws one, and `steerSlime` moves it each step: on the floor it brakes, rests,\n * crouches and leaps; in the air it flies on until it lands.\n *\n * Its hop, the prototype's: after a rest it crouches for `SLIME.crouch`, then leaps (`hop`, engine/world/steer.ts)\n * `SLIME.reach` metres along the flow field toward the hero's tile, up at `SLIME.up` m/s, so it lands where it aimed\n * under its own gravity, onto a stair as well as across the floor; level with the hero it keeps to a ring round him\n * instead, leaping in from beyond it by what it lacks and out from inside it. A hop too short to bother with, or one\n * out of reach, waits a moment. After landing it rests for `SLIME.rest` plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`, drawn from the\n * crowd's stream.\n *\n * Its pounce (Box 5, WP 6.7): `SLIME_ATTACK`. Resting on its ring round the hero, cooled down and granted one of his\n * attack tokens, it squats for `wind` s, its line telegraph (`telegraph:boxPounce`) filling toward him, then leaps at\n * where he stood, up at `up` m/s, to land just short of him; touching him on the way takes `damage` hit points and\n * throws it back off him. Landed, it gives the token back and rests `rest` s plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`. A hit on\n * it breaks its pounce off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's slime (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:200-203, 387-414`), in SI units\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical): a ball of radius 6 units\n * → 0.375 m; leaps of 150 units/s up → 9.375 m/s (`HOP.up`), at most 44 units → 2.75 m (`HOP.reach`), after a crouch\n * of 0.28 s; a rest of 0.45 s plus up to 0.6 s; braking at 400 units/s² → 25 m/s²; its ring 34 units → 2.125 m, its\n * band 8 units → 0.5 m. Its first rest is drawn from its spawn, up to 1 s.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as a blob (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `SLIME.looks`, squashed by where it\n * is in its hop (`SLIME.squash`); the blob's spring makes the bounce.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * SLIME.reach; // 2.75: m, its longest hop\n * // steerSlime(physics, agent, slime, chase); // in the phase ai, each step\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  HOP,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineTelegraph,\n  followFlow,\n  hop,\n  knockback,\n  launch,\n  setVelocity,\n  Vector3,\n  type CrowdAgent,\n  type Physics,\n  type Rng,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { levelWith, type Chase } from './walker';\n\n/** The prototype's units per metre (PLAN.md Appendix C). */\nconst UNITS = 16;\n\n/** The slime's numbers (see the file comment). */\nexport const SLIME = Object.freeze({\n  /** Its body: a ball (m). */\n  agent: Object.freeze({ shape: 'ball', radius: 6 / UNITS } as const),\n  /** How fast it leaps up (m/s), and its longest leap (m). */\n  up: HOP.up,\n  reach: HOP.reach,\n  /** A leap shorter than this (m) is not worth it: it waits `SLIME.wait` instead. */\n  least: 4 / UNITS,\n  /** Seconds it crouches before a leap, waits after a leap it skipped, and rests after landing (plus a spread). */\n  crouch: 0.28,\n  wait: 0.3,\n  rest: 0.45,\n  restSpread: 0.6,\n  /** In the air at least this long (s) before it can land. */\n  airborne: 0.1,\n  /** How hard it brakes on the floor (m/s²). */\n  brake: 400 / UNITS,\n  /** The ring it keeps round the hero (m), and its band either side (m). */\n  ring: Object.freeze({ radius: 34 / UNITS, band: 8 / UNITS }),\n  /** Its looks, one drawn per slime: the prototype's `SLIME_PARTS`, plain twice, horns, cat ears, wings. */\n  looks: Object.freeze(['', '', 'horns', 'ears', 'wings']),\n  /** The squash its body eases to (engine/anim/blob.ts): flat in its crouch, stretched rising, braced falling. */\n  squash: Object.freeze({ rest: 0, crouch: -0.35, rising: 0.25, falling: -0.1 }),\n});","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01639uErW9Bu11dm3if4Kw2r","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
