ks like (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in\n * INDEX). It starts as the scenery in 24 shades a channel, softly dithered, the characters and objects inked, the\n * whole picture a little warmer.\n *\n * Invariants: data only, the kind's fields (`node x describe look`): the filters it turns on, each with its scope\n * (all, characters, objects, environment, or two joined by '+') and numbers, every filter left out off; and a\n * material style (`style`: lambert, toon, flat, pbr), which only a page whose chain has a style set applies (advice\n * `GFX_POST_NO_STYLES` otherwise; '' keeps the scene's own). Levels are 0 (off) or 8 and more (24 suits pixel art),\n * so dull colours keep their hue. It may lay other looks on first (`combine`: each a look, an `amount` and `only` some\n * of its filters; its own filters that are on go over them) and fade the whole (`strength`). A page draws it when its\n * setting `post.look` names it; `__engine.look()` there gives the filters it draws.\n *\n * @example\n * look.id; // 'look:{{name}}'\n * @see {{id}}.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineLook } from '../../../engine';\n\n/** The look `look:{{name}}`: replace this sentence with what it looks like. */\nexport const look = defineLook('look:{{name}}', {\n  description: 'The scenery in 24 soft shades, the characters and objects inked, the picture warmer (replace).',\n  style: '',\n  filters: {\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 2, darken: 0 },\n    palette: { scope: 'environment', levels: 24, dither: 0.3 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.2, saturation: 1.1 },\n  },\n  combine: [{ look: 'look:vignette/soft', amount: 0.8 }], // looks laid on under its own filters\n  strength: 1, // how much of the whole look shows\n  gallery: { camera: 'front', duration: 0, states: [] }, // node x gallery: the gallery's set in it\n});\n/**\n * @file The action `action:{{name}}`: what sequence it is (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\