{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EsVKS6dT9tRFe3qXPTsPVd","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file Actors on the stage (PLAN.md WP 3.10, §6.4's view; I-21): every actor with an animator (engine/sim/actors.ts:\n * an entity with the components `actor` and `animator`) drawn as a puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts) of the neutral\n * humanoid (`ACTOR_BODY`) or the body its component `puppet` names (`body:mannequin`, WP 8.9), in its animator's build,\n * posed every frame by its animator's presentation half (engine/anim/character.ts `pose`) at the frame's alpha; an\n * actor with clips (`clips`, engine/sim/actorClips.ts) has its clip layer laid over the body, loaded from the same data\n * (a `ClipLayerPool` of the view's own, engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts). The stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) draws these.\n *\n * `capture(entities, dt, queries)` after each sim step keeps each actor's last two places (feet and heading) and its\n * animator's data; `draw(alpha)` poses each puppet `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last. `player()` is\n * the first player actor (in id order) as the last draw put it: its feet and, with a puppet, its skeleton, world pose\n * and eye (the head socket, engine/gfx/cameras/first.ts's `eyePoint`), which the cameras follow (engine/app/view.ts).\n * `firstPerson(frame)` draws the player for a first-person camera's frame (engine/gfx/viewmodel/body.ts, WP 13.12:\n * his body hidden, its shadow kept, his arms posed against it by a lens of their own), or whole for null. `trails()` is\n * each puppet's trail as its last pose sampled it (WP 6.7, oldest first), which the stage's effects draw as ribbons.\n * WP 13.20: the weapon an actor has out stands in its right hand while its hold holds a gun (`carried`, `muzzle`).\n * WP 10.2: a `ragdoll` (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts) lays its parts on the bones, faded in and out (`layRagdoll`).\n *\n * WP 6.2 in the box (WP 7.8): an actor's `reactions` (engine/sim/reactions.ts) are a `Reactions` layer on its puppet's\n * animator, loaded at every pose (its flinch bends its spine; a body down on its face is drawn so), its `actions` (WP\n * 13.11, engine/sim/actorActions.ts) an `Actions` layer on its clip layer, its `secondary` a `Secondary` layer whose\n * chains hang under the puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/chains.ts: `actor#<id>/cape`…), and its `post` slot ends with a\n * `FootPlant` (engine/anim/footPlant.ts) on the ground the sim's `queries` find, faded out as far as its clips hold its\n * legs (clipsets.ts `legsHeld`). WP 13.10: an actor's movement (`motion`) shows on its body (motion.ts `MovementPose`)\n * and locks its feet as `plantsFeet` lets it, laid as the feel kit's (anim/bodyPlants.ts); its layers: actorLayers.ts.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only (doctrine: WebGPU only): its animators and their layers are its own, loaded from the\n * sim's data at every pose and never writing it, so drawing, culling or not drawing never changes the hash (the\n * animator's own invariant, engine/anim/character.test.ts); one puppet per actor, its layers made again when its\n * animator or their components do; every object it draws is under `root`, and a puppet given up waits as a spare for\n * the next actor of its build and body (`createActorPuppets` says why). A puppet is a skinned mesh of two draw calls:\n * right for heroes and a few foes; crowds draw through instanced batches (WP 5.4).\n *\n * @example\n * // const actors = createActorPuppets({ materials: library }); stage.scene.add(actors.root);\n * // const drawn = actors.capture(world.query('actor'), world.dt); // the ids drawn as puppets\n * // actors.draw(0.5);\n * // actors.player()?.eye; // where a first-person camera sits\n * @see engine/gfx/puppets/actors.test.ts\n */\n71:import { compileBody } from './compile';\n206:    puppet = spares.get(key)?.pop() ?? createPuppet(compileBody(body, data.build, { registry }), { materials: options.materials, name: `actor#${id}` }); // prettier-ignore\n237:        const body = (entity.puppet as { body?: string } | undefined)?.body ?? ACTOR_BODY;\n343:          objects: () => [...[...puppets.values()].flatMap((puppet) => [puppet.mesh, ...(viewmodels.has(puppet) ? [viewmodels.get(puppet)!.arms, ...viewmodels.get(puppet)!.guns.values()] : [])]), ...chains()], // prettier-ignore\n346:          const bodies = [...puppets.values()].map((puppet) => {\n361:      for (const puppet of [...puppets.values(), ...[...spares.values()].flat()]) puppet.dispose();\n/**\n * @file The stage's stand-ins (engine/gfx/stage.ts, PLAN.md WP 2.7): which entities stand somewhere and where. An entity\n * is drawn as a box when one of its components declares `x` and `z` as numbers in metres (`placeableKinds`, asked of\n * the entries, never of a name); the first such component in registry order places it (`placeOf`): `x`, `y` (the\n * box's bottom, 0 by default) and `z`, `yaw` (rad), `size` (the box's side, m; 0.5 by default) and `material` (a\n * material library id; `material:default` otherwise). Split from stage.ts at its line cap.\n *\n * Invariants: pure reads of the registry and the entity's data; a field that is not a finite number takes its default.\n *\n * @example\n * placeOf({ id: 1, dot: { x: 2, z: 3, size: 0 } }, ['dot']); // { kind: 'dot', place: { x: 2, y: 0, z: 3, yaw: 0, size: 0.5, material: 'material:default' } }\n * @see engine/gfx/stage.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { Field } from '../core/schema';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\n\n/** Where a stand-in stands and how it looks, read from its entity's placing component. */\nexport interface StandInPlace {\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n  z: number;\n  yaw: number;\n  size: number;\n  material: string;\n}\n\n/** A side for a stand-in that declares none, m. */\nconst DEFAULT_SIZE = 0.5;\n\nexport interface TelegraphPlace {\n  /** The telegraph's id. */\n  readonly telegraph: string;\n  /** Where it stands: its origin, on the floor (y is the floor's height). */\n  readonly position: PointLike;\n  /** Its facing, rad; forward is (sin yaw, 0, cos yaw). */\n  readonly yaw: number;\n  /** How far its wind-up has run, 0 to 1. */\n  readonly u: number;\n  /** Scales every length (a big attacker's reach); 1 by default. */\n  readonly size?: number;\n}\n  readonly u: number;\n  /** Scales every length (a big attacker's reach); 1 by default. */\n  readonly size?: number;\n}\n\n/** The kind's own entries: one generic shape each. */\nconst BUILT_IN: Record<string, TelegraphSpec> = {\n  'telegraph:arc': {\n    description: \"A swing's warning: from near the attacker out to its reach, 0.8 rad either side of its facing.\",\n    shape: 'arc',\n    inner: 0.3,\n    radius: 1.5,\n  },\n  'telegraph:ring': {\n    description: 'A slam or a blast: the floor all round, out to its radius.',\n    shape: 'ring',\n    radius: 2,\n  },\n  'telegraph:line': {\n    description: 'A charge or a beam: a strip a metre wide, 4 m forward.',\n    shape: 'line',\n    length: 4,\n    width: 1,\n  },\n  'telegraph:cone': {\n    description: 'A thrust or a breath: the floor from the attacker out to its reach, 0.5 rad either side.',\n    shape: 'cone',\n    radius: 2,\n    halfAngle: 0.5,\n  },\n};\n\n/** A colour: `#rgb` or `#rrggbb`. */\nconst HEX = /^#([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i;\n\n/** The problems of a telegraph beyond its fields. */\nfunction telegraphProblems(t: Telegraph): string[] {\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  if (t.shape !== 'line' && !(t.radius > 0)) problems.push(`a ${t.shape} needs a radius above 0`);\n  if ((t.shape === 'arc' || t.shape === 'ring') && t.inner >= t.radius) {\n    problems.push(`inner ${t.inner} is not below radius ${t.radius}: the ${t.shape} would be empty`);\n  }\n  if (t.shape === 'line' && !(t.length > 0 && t.width > 0)) problems.push('a line needs a length and a width above 0');\n  if (t.yMin >= t.yMax) problems.push(`yMin ${t.yMin} is not below yMax ${t.yMax}`);\n  if (t.alpha.length !== 2) problems.push(`alpha has ${t.alpha.length} numbers; it is [start, end]`);\n  if (!HEX.test(t.color)) problems.push(`color \"${t.color}\" is not a hex colour ('#ff4a3a')`);\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `telegraph` on `registry`, with its four shapes, unless it has it. */\nexport function telegraphKind(registry: Registry): void {\nconst BUILT_IN: Record<string, TelegraphSpec> = {\n  'telegraph:arc': {\n    description: \"A swing's warning: from near the attacker out to its reach, 0.8 rad either side of its facing.\",\n    shape: 'arc',\n    inner: 0.3,\n    radius: 1.5,\n  },\n  'telegraph:ring': {\n    description: 'A slam or a blast: the floor all round, out to its radius.',\n    shape: 'ring',\n    radius: 2,\n  },\n  'telegraph:line': {\n    description: 'A charge or a beam: a strip a metre wide, 4 m forward.',\n    shape: 'line',\n    length: 4,\n    width: 1,\n  },\n  'telegraph:cone': {\n    description: 'A thrust or a breath: the floor from the attacker out to its reach, 0.5 rad either side.',\n    shape: 'cone',\n    radius: 2,\n    halfAngle: 0.5,\n  },\n};\n/**\n * @file Terrain (PLAN.md WP 10.5, §5.8; docs/PLAYGROUND.md §2.2, §6.3): outdoor ground as plain data, a heightfield\n * made from a seeded spec, and the queries on it. `defineTerrain(id, spec)` registers a spec (the registry kind\n * `terrain`); `getTerrain(id)` makes it (`makeTerrain`): a grid of `cols` × `rows` cells `cell` metres wide from its\n * north-west corner `origin`, a height at every cell corner. The physics stands it as a heightfield\n * (engine/sim/levelBodies.ts's `addTerrainBody`, engine/physics/heightfield.ts), the view draws it in chunks\n * (engine/gfx/terrain.ts), navigation walks it (engine/world/terrainNav.ts).\n *\n * A height is shardfall's: fbm value noise of `height` metres' range at the `scale` of its features, plus a ridged\n * fbm (`ridges` of it), then the `hills` (smooth domes, each `height` high and `radius` across from `at`) added, then\n * rounded to `terrace` steps when that is set, then pulled to each of the `flats` (a footprint flattened to its\n * `height`, blending back over `margin` metres round it), all over `origin`'s height. Cells split as Rapier splits a\n * heightfield's: along the diagonal from the north-east corner to the south-west one, so `terrainHeight` is the\n * collider's surface, the triangle under the point interpolated, and `terrainNormal` that triangle's normal.\n *\n * `surface` is the tag underfoot, `steepSurface` where the ground rises `steep` metres a metre or more (0.7: 35°);\n * `materials` (presentation only, as a level's) are the drawing's layers: the ground, the steep and, from `high`\n * metres over the origin up (0: none), the high one. `scatterTerrain` places trees and rocks by hashes of the cells\n * (shardfall's stateless placement).\n *\n * Invariants: pure: equal specs give equal terrains in Node and Chromium (int32 hashing, polynomial blends, no trig);\n * heights are float32, as the collider keeps them; outside the grid nothing stands (`terrainHeight` is null).\n *\n * Carried from shardfall@fa2dab6 `crates/pav_core/src/terrain.rs:93-153` (`raw_height`: fbm of 5 octaves at\n * lacunarity 2.03, the ridge term, the flattened footprints' smoothstep, `cell`'s terraces; `decor`'s hashed cells),\n * as a concept: on a heightfield's corners rather than in terraced tiles.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * const reg = createRegistry();\n * defineTerrain('terrain:knoll', { size: [16, 16], hills: [{ at: [8, 8], radius: 8, height: 2 }] }, reg);\n * const knoll = getTerrain('terrain:knoll', reg);\n * [knoll.cols, terrainHeight(knoll, 8, 8), terrainHeight(knoll, 0, 0), terrainHeight(knoll, -1, 0)]; // [16, 2, 0, null]\n * @see engine/world/terrain.test.ts\n */\nimport { mix32 } from '../core/hash';\nimport { codeError } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { createNoise2D } from '../core/noise';\nimport { Vector3 } from '../core/math';\nimport type { Schema, SpecOf } from '../core/schema';\n\n/** A two-number field (m). */\nconst pair = (description: string, required = false) =>\n  ({ type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, ...(required ? { required } : { default: [0, 0] }), unit: 'm', description }) as const; // prettier-ignore\n\n/** The fields of a `terrain` entry (see the file comment). */\nexport const TERRAIN_FIELDS = {\n  size: pair('Its extent along x and along z, each a whole number of cells: [24, 96].', true),\n  cell: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0.25, maximum: 8, unit: 'm', description: 'The grid’s spacing: a height stands at every cell’s corners.' }, // prettier-ign\nexport interface TerrainHill {\n  readonly at: readonly [number, number];\n  readonly radius: number;\n  readonly height: number;\n}\nexport interface TerrainFlat {\n  readonly rect: readonly [x0: number, z0: number, x1: number, z1: number];\n  readonly height: number;\n  readonly margin: number;\n}\nengine/sim/levelBodies.ts:76:export function addTerrainBody(physics: Physics, terrain: Terrain, cut?: Uint8Array | null): number {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"fca9786e-4a68-4ad3-b772-63eecf2792fd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:58:12.988Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file Actors on the stage (PLAN.md WP 3.10, §6.4's view; I-21): every actor with an animator (engine/sim/actors.ts:\n * an entity with the components `actor` and `animator`) drawn as a puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts) of the neutral\n * humanoid (`ACTOR_BODY`) or the body its component `puppet` names (`body:mannequin`, WP 8.9), in its animator's build,\n * posed every frame by its animator's presentation half (engine/anim/character.ts `pose`) at the frame's alpha; an\n * actor with clips (`clips`, engine/sim/actorClips.ts) has its clip layer laid over the