{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F8ViYGzSjGm7aHrf3oqQtM","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file Props on the stage (PLAN.md WP 4.6 core proposal, ADR-0008 amendment 5; §6.4's view): every entity with the\n * component `sceneProp` (engine/sim/props.ts: a prop standing in a scene, its id and its pose) drawn as its prop\n * through the prop meshes (engine/gfx/props.ts: one instanced batch per prop part, so a hundred crates are one draw\n * call), where its pose is at the frame's alpha. The stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) draws these instead of stand-ins.\n *\n * `capture(entities, dt)` after each sim step keeps each prop's last two poses (centre and turn) and returns the ids\n * it draws; `draw(alpha)` draws each `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last (the centre along the line,\n * the turn the shorter way round), at presentation time (the steps captured, `alpha` of a step on), on which the\n * flames dance; each prop is drawn under its entity id, so its flames keep their own phase, and on or off as its\n * `propLight` says (a lamp its switch turned off: WP 13.16); `hide(test, key)` leaves out those on a storey the cut\n * takes off (engine/gfx/storeyCut.ts), lights and all, and says when its key changed. `lights()` lists this frame's\n * light spots in world space (the brazier's torch, the lamps that are on), for the light pool (WP 7.1). `carry(guns)`\n * adds the guns in the actors' hands (engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts `carried`, WP 13.20) to the draws after it, each as\n * its weapon's prop where its grip stands, never hidden by the cut (its actor is not).\n *\n * The prop meshes are made when the first prop arrives, with a batch for every registered prop, and added to the\n * stage's scene then: a stage with no prop has none, and its scene graph is the one it had before props. `register`\n * registers their batches with the warm-up and adds whether there are any to the shader key, so the frame after they\n * arrive warms up first instead of stalling.\n *\n * Invariants: presentation only (doctrine: WebGPU only): it reads the components and writes nothing back; equal\n * captures and alphas give equal matrices; every object it makes is under the prop meshes' root.\n *\n * @example\n * // const props = createStageProps({ scene: stage.scene, materials: library });\n * // const drawn = props.capture(world.query('sceneProp'), world.dt); // the ids drawn as props\n * // props.draw(0.5); // halfway between the last two steps\n * @see engine/gfx/stageProps.test.ts\n */\nimport { Quaternion, Vector3, type Material, type Scene } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport type { EntityData } from '../sim/state';\nimport { createPropMeshes, type PropLight, type PropMeshes } from './props';\nimport type { Warmup } from './warmup';\nimport type { HeldGun } from './weapons';\n\n/** What `createStageProps` takes. */\nexport interface StagePropsOptions {\n  /** The scene the prop meshes join when the first prop arrives. */\n  scene: Scene;\n  /** Where the materials come from: the page's material library. */\n  materials: { get(id: string): Material };\n  /** Where the props are declared (the shared registry by default). */\n  registry?: Registry;\n}\n\n/** A prop's pose: its centre (m) and its turn. */\ninterface Pose {\n  p: [number, number, number];\n  q: [number, number, number, number];\n}\n\n/** What the module keeps of one prop: its poses, and whether it is on (its `propLight`'s; true without one). */\ninterface Held {\n  prop: string;\n  before: Pose;\n  after: Pose;\n  on: boolean;\n}\nfunction readProps(w: World): void {\n  const physics = physicsOf(w);\n  for (const { sceneProp } of w.query('sceneProp') as unknown as ScenePropComponents[]) {\n    if (sceneProp.body < 0) continue;\n    const { position: p, rotation: r } = physics.readBody(sceneProp.body);\n    [sceneProp.x, sceneProp.y, sceneProp.z] = [p.x, p.y, p.z];\n    sceneProp.q = [r.x, r.y, r.z, r.w];\n  }\n}\nexport function removeProp<C extends object, E extends EventMap>(world: World<C, E>, id: number): void {\n  const w = world as unknown as World;\n  const data = propOf(w, id, 'removeProp(w, id)');\n  if (data.body >= 0) physicsOf(w).removeBody(data.body);\n  data.body = -1; // inside a step its entity stays to the step's end: nothing reads the body it no longer has\n  w.despawn(id);\n}\nawk: fatal: cannot open file `engine/world/props.ts' for reading: No such file or directory\nawk: fatal: cannot open file `engine/world/props.ts' for reading: No such file or directory\nawk: fatal: cannot open file `engine/world/props.ts' for reading: No such file or directory\nx describe: ok: geometry: 4 fields, 7 entries\nShapes props, levels and bodies name by id: a builder of a three.js BufferGeometry with its parameters and a vertex budg\nfallback: geometry:box\nids: geometry:box, geometry:frustum, geometry:limb, geometry:pillar, geometry:ramp, geometry:ring, geometry:roundedBox\n  description: string, required: What it is, in plain sentences.\n  params: object, = {}: Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, description, minimum…), e\n  budget: integer, = 4096, 1..inf: The most vertices it may have at its default parameters (the geo QA family checks it)\n  create: function, required: The builder: (params) => BufferGeometry, standing on the ground, in metres, with normals a\n(a line above is cut short: the whole text is in out/describe/geometry/describe.json)\nreport: out/describe/geometry/report.json\nx describe: ok: material: 18 fields, 29 entries\nMaterials as data with three.js's classic parameters (color, map, roughness, emissive, flags); the e\nfallback: material:default\nids: material:asphalt, material:barrel, material:barrelLid, material:barrelStaves, material:blobShad\n  description: string, = \"\": What it is for, in plain sentences.\n  color: string, = \"#ffffff\": The base colour, hex; it multiplies the map (three.js's color).\n  map: any, = null: The texture generator that fills the maps: a texture id ('texture:brick'), or { \n  roughness: number, = 1, 0..1: Microfacet roughness, 0 (mirror) to 1 (matte), for the styles that s\n  metalness: number, = 0, 0..1: How metallic, 0 to 1, for the styles that shade with it (pbr, WP 7.2\n  emissive: string, = \"#000000\": The colour it glows with, hex, unaffected by light; it multiplies t\n  emissiveIntensity: number, = 1, 0..inf: A multiplier on emissive.\n  normalScale: number, = 1, 0..8: How deep the map's relief looks: scales the normal map from its he\n  unlit: boolean, = false: Drawn without lights (glTF unlit, three.js MeshBasicMaterial): color × ma\n  transparent: boolean, = false: Blended with what is behind it, by opacity.\n  opacity: number, = 1, 0..1: Its opacity when transparent.\n  alphaTest: number, = 0, 0..1: Texels with alpha below this are not drawn (cut-outs).\n  side: string, = \"front\", one of \"front\"|\"back\"|\"double\": Which faces are drawn.\n  flatShading: boolean, = false: Faceted: one normal per triangle.\n… 5 more in out/describe/material/output.txt\nreport: out/describe/material/report.json\nx describe: ok: texture: 7 fields, 24 entries\nSeeded, periodic texture generators: colour, height, roughness and emissive per texel, with their pa\nids: texture:asphalt, texture:brick, texture:carpet, texture:checker, texture:concrete, texture:crat\n  description: string, required: What it draws, in plain sentences.\n  params: object, = {}: Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, descr\n  size: array, = [64,64]: The size it bakes at, [width, height] in texels: a whole number of tiles.\n  tile: function, = function: The smallest size its pattern repeats at, given the parameters: (param\n  density: number, = 16, 0.001..inf, texels/m: Texels per metre on geometry whose UVs are in metres \n  look: string, = \"pixel\", one of \"pixel\"|\"smooth\": How it is magnified: 'pixel' keeps texels crisp \n  create: function, required: The generator: ({ params, seed, width, height }) => (x, y, texel) => v\n(a line above is cut short: the whole text is in out/describe/texture/describe.json)\nreport: out/describe/texture/report.json\nx describe: ok: emitter: 28 fields, 27 entries\nEmitters: particle effects as data (how particles start, move and look), burst where something happe\nfallback: emitter:sparks\nids: emitter:bits, emitter:block, emitter:bubbles, emitter:confetti, emitter:destroyed, emitter:dust\n  description: string, = \"\": What it is, in plain sentences.\n  area: array, = [0,0,0], m: Half extents of the box particles start in, around where it bursts.\n  velocity: array, = [0,0,0], m/s: Every particle's starting velocity.\n  spread: number, = 1, 0..inf, m/s: Random extra speed in any direction, up to this.\n  gravity: number, = 0, m/s²: Pulls particles down; below 0 they rise.\n  drag: number, = 0, 0..inf, 1/s: Slows them: the share of their speed lost per second.\n  turbulence: number, = 0, 0..inf, m/s²: Swirls them (smoke, fireflies).\n  life: array, = [1,1.5], s: The shortest and longest a particle lives.\n  size: array, = [0.1,0], m: Its radius at birth and at death.\n  color: array, = [\"#ffffff\",\"#ffffff\"]: Its colour at birth and at death, hex.\n  brightness: array, = [1,1]: What each colour is multiplied by, linear: above 1 it glows (with bloo\n  alpha: array, = [1,0]: Its opacity at birth and at death, 0 to 1.\n  additive: boolean, = true: Adds light (fire, sparks, magic) instead of covering.\n  stretch: boolean, = false: Streaks along its velocity (sparks, rain).\n… 15 more in out/describe/emitter/output.txt\nreport: out/describe/emitter/report.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"15995e34-2954-4752-a449-5f36866f2743","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:59:15.534Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file Props on the stage (PLAN.md WP 4.6