{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DRCY3i1kbv8DJipbmfzL3s","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The chase camera (PLAN.md WP 3.9, §6.1; doctrine: Common ground, Quality under the hood): a perspective camera\n * on a spring arm behind and above the hero, turned by the devices, that slides in front of a wall rather than through\n * it, as Unreal's spring arm and Cinemachine's third-person follow do. `stepChase` and `chasePose` are the pure steps;\n * `createChaseCamera` wraps them in a camera.\n *\n * The arm hangs from a pivot `CHASE_HEIGHT` above `input.follow` (the hero's feet), which follows with a time constant\n * of `CHASE_LAG` real seconds, and runs back against the view direction (`yaw`, `pitch`) for `distance`. `input.look`\n * and `input.turn` turn the view right and up; `input.zoom` steps the arm in by `ORBIT_ZOOM_STEP`.\n *\n * Walls (engine/gfx/cameras/collide.ts): through the sim's read-only `QueryView` (`input.queries`), a ball of\n * `CHASE_RADIUS` is swept from the hero's head (the pivot before its lag) to the pivot, then cast along the arm, and\n * stops short of the first surface of `input.groups` (`world` by default; `input.exclude` skips his own body). The arm\n * snaps in at once and eases back out with a time constant of `CHASE_RETURN`, never past what the casts left clear.\n * Without `queries` nothing shortens it.\n *\n * Invariants: with `queries`, and the hero's head at least `CHASE_RADIUS` from every wall (a character's capsule is\n * wider), the camera's ball, so its near plane, never ends inside a wall, and the line from the head to the camera is\n * clear (chase.test.ts walks fixtures/scenes/chase-walls/ to prove it). The pitch stays within `CHASE_LIMITS.pitch`,\n * the arm within `CHASE_LIMITS.distance`. Pure: each step returns a new state.\n *\n * Codes: `cam3=chase[,<yaw>,<pitch>,<distance>]` (degrees, metres; a bare one keeps the last camera's heading). Until\n * codes.ts reads WP 3.9's cameras, this file holds what they share: `readCode`, `codeNumber`, `followCamera`.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/40-cameras.js:84-94` (`chasePose`: the arm, its pitch, lens and lag, the\n * pull in front of a wall) and `:37` (its numbers), in metres and +Y up, the height-map march replaced by ball casts.\n *\n * @example\n * import { startScene } from '../../sim/scene';\n * import { queryViewOf } from '../../sim/queryView';\n * import chaseWalls from '../../../fixtures/scenes/chase-walls';\n * const chase = createChaseCamera();\n * const pose = chase.update({ follow: [2, 0, 3] }, 1 / 60); // the first follow snaps to the hero\n * pose.position; // [2, 3.44…, -2.15…]: 5.5 m back from 1.5 m above his feet, looking along +Z and 20.6° down\n * chase.code(); // 'cam3=chase,0,-20.63,5.5'\n * const { world } = startScene(chaseWalls);\n * world.step({}); // queries see the level from the first step\n * createChaseCamera().update({ follow: [1.5, 0, 1.5], queries: queryViewOf(world) }).distance; // 0.299…: a wall behind\n * @see engine/gfx/cameras/chase.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, didYouMean } from '../../core/log';\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\nimport { COLLIDE_RADIUS, COLLIDE_RETURN, COLLIDE_SKIN, easeArm, reach, sweep, type Walls } from './collide';\nimport type { EffectWeights } from './effects';\nimport { ORBIT_ZOOM_STEP } from './orbit';\nimport {\n  approach,\n  makePose,\n  poseForward,\n  rangeProblems,\nexport interface CameraInput {\n  /** Look this frame `[right, up]`, rad: turn the view right and tilt it up (a captured mouse × its sensitivity). */\n  readonly look?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** Turn rates `[right, up]`, −1 to 1 (arrow keys, a right stick), times the camera's turn speed. */\n  readonly turn?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** Move axes `[right, forward, up]`, −1 to 1 (WASD, then E or Space up and Q down): fly cameras. */\n  readonly move?: readonly [number, number, number];\n  /** Move at the fast speed (Shift). */\n  readonly fast?: boolean;\n  /** Zoom steps, + in (wheel notches, + and −): views step their zoom, orbits come closer, fly and fixed narrow. */\n  readonly zoom?: number;\n  /** 45° turns of a classic view, + raising its azimuth (the prototype's `]` key). */\n  readonly turnSteps?: number;\n  /** The zoom steps a classic view's `zoom` moves through (engine/gfx/cameras/presets.ts's when absent). */\n  readonly zooms?: readonly number[];\n  /** The point views and orbits follow (the hero's feet, or a point just ahead of his aim), m. */\n  readonly follow?: Vec3;\n}\nengine/app/engine.ts:11: * view drawn at the clock's alpha; the map follows the camera, the look the view settings `input.*`, the aim the\nengine/app/engine.ts:27: * still read the system layer, but no intent reaches the run; `cameraInput()` is laid over each frame's camera input.\nengine/app/engine.ts:144:  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\nengine/app/engine.ts:221:  const parts: PageParts = { run: null, gfx: null, post: null, look: null, input: null, layer: null, ui: null, numbers: null, governor: createGovernor({ log, memory: governorMemory(options.store, () => routes?.scene) }), cameraInput: options.cameraInput, ready: false }; // prettier-ignore\nengine/app/view.ts:16: * follows the player (WP 3.10): the first player actor's feet as the frame draws them, else the level's middle; so does\nengine/app/view.ts:19: * a physics scene (the follow cameras keep out of the walls and the doors standing shut), the player's eye (the shooter model's height, else his\nengine/app/view.ts:136:   * Moves the camera by one rendered frame and the stand-ins to `alpha`; returns what to draw. The stage's sky follows,\nengine/app/view.ts:217:  /** The sim's read-only queries, for the follow cameras' walls and the puppets' ground; none without physics. */\nengine/app/view.ts:229:  /** The doors standing shut after the last step, which stop the follow cameras as walls do (engine/sim/doors.ts). 