{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JaMdG69MS3ow7Hi43dW8Lc","type":"tool_result","content":"7: * - `JOINTS` lists parents before children; `PARENTS[j]` is −1 for the pelvis, whose parent is the root.\n8- * - The rest pose is a T-pose with every local rotation the identity: each joint's frame is the character's, and the\n9- *   offsets alone shape it (arms out along ±X, legs straight down, soles on the floor at y = 0). A joint sits at its\n10- *   parent's frame times its offset, as a three.js `Bone` sits at its `position`.\n11- * - Lengths are metres, the build's times its `size`. `legUpper + legLower` reaches from the hip joint to the sole,\n12- *   so the pelvis rests at that height. The proportions the old rig lacked (spine split, clavicles, feet, eyes, grip)\n13- *   are shares of build lengths in `PROPORTIONS`.\n14- * - Names follow Appendix C: `JOINT_INFO` gives each joint's old `rig.J` key and the mocap points it stands for.\n15- *\n--\n35:    doc: 'Raised by `jointIndex`, `socketIndex`, `boneMask` and the pose functions that take a joint (engine/anim/) for a name the skeleton lacks, or a joint\n36-  },\n37-  ANIM_BAD_MASK: {\n38-    template: 'the bone mask weight of {name} is {value}',\n39-    fix: 'give each weight a number from 0 to 1',\n40-    doc: 'Raised by `boneMask` (engine/anim/skeleton.ts) for a weight that is not a number from 0 to 1.',\n41-  },\n42-});\n43-\n--\n45:export const JOINTS = [\n46-  'pelvis',\n47-  'spine0',\n48-  'spine1',\n49-  'spine2',\n50-  'chest',\n51-  'neck',\n52-  'head',\n53-  'clavicleL',\n--\n72:export type JointName = (typeof JOINTS)[number];\n73-\n74-/** How many joints a pose holds: 23. */\n75:export const JOINT_COUNT = JOINTS.length;\n76-\n77-/** What Appendix C says of a joint: its parent, the old rig's `rig.J` key, and the mocap points it stands for. */\n78-export interface JointInfo {\n79-  readonly parent: JointName | 'root';\n80-  readonly rig?: string;\n81-  readonly mocap: readonly string[];\n35:    doc: 'Raised by `jointIndex`, `socketIndex`, `boneMask` and the pose functions that take a joint (engine/anim/) for a name the skeleton lacks, or a joint index out\n36-  },\n37-  ANIM_BAD_MASK: {\n38-    template: 'the bone mask weight of {name} is {value}',\n39-    fix: 'give each weight a number from 0 to 1',\n40-    doc: 'Raised by `boneMask` (engine/anim/skeleton.ts) for a weight that is not a number from 0 to 1.',\n41-  },\n--\n118:export const SOCKETS = ['weaponR', 'weaponL', 'headTop', 'eyeL', 'eyeR', 'contactL', 'contactR', 'back'] as const;\n119-\n120-/** A socket's name. */\n121:export type SocketName = (typeof SOCKETS)[number];\n122-\n123-/** The joint each socket rides on. A weapon's blade runs along its socket's +Z (the thumb side of a fist). */\n124-export const SOCKET_JOINTS: Readonly<Record<SocketName, JointName>> = {\n125-  weaponR: 'handR',\n126-  weaponL: 'handL',\n127-  headTop: 'head',\n--\n173:  /** Each socket's joint index, in `SOCKETS` order. */\n174-  readonly socketJoints: readonly number[];\n175-  /** Each socket's position in its joint's frame, 3 per socket. */\n176-  readonly socketOffsets: Float64Array;\n177-  /** Rest height: the soles to the top of the head. */\nengine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts engine/gfx/puppets/actors.ts engine/gfx/puppets/compile.ts\nx describe: ok: material \"material:puppet\": 3 of 18 fields differ from the default\n* description = \"A puppet, lit: white, multiplied by each part’s slot colour (vertex or instance colours).\"\n  color = \"#ffffff\"\n  map = null\n* roughness = 0.8\n  metalness = 0\n  emissive = \"#000000\"\n  emissiveIntensity = 1\n  normalScale = 1\n  unlit = false\n  transparent = false\n  opacity = 1\n  alphaTest = 0\n  side = \"front\"\nids: material:asphalt, material:barrel, material:barrelLid, material:barrelStaves, material:blobShadow, material:brick, material:carpet, material:checker, material:cloth, material:concrete, material:crate, material:default, material:flagst