{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsUKj19PWTDo3gRK83QHTy","type":"tool_result","content":"// T0 project: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: the labs, the fixtures, the tools, the test pages,\n// specs and helpers, the Claude Code hooks and the root configs (tsconfig.check.json).\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"composite\": true,\n    \"emitDeclarationOnly\": true,\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"outDir\": \"node_modules/.cache/tsc\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"labs\", \"fixtures\", \"tools\", \"tests\", \".claude/hooks\", \"*.config.ts\", \"package-lock.json\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"**/*.test.ts\"],\n  \"references\": [{ \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" }]\n}\n// T0's type check (`npm run typecheck`, inside `npm run check`): `tsc -b` over three composite projects that emit\n// declarations only, into node_modules/.cache/tsc/. A run skips a project whose own files and upstream declarations\n// did not change, and re-checks only what a change can reach (ADR-0014, amendment 7). Together the projects hold\n// exactly tsconfig.json's files, each once (tools/checkAll.test.ts checks it):\n// - tsconfig.engine.json: engine/, without its tests. The engine imports nothing outside it (PLAN.md §6.1).\n// - tsconfig.apps.json: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: labs/, fixtures/, tools/, tests/ (pages,\n//   specs, setup, helpers), .claude/hooks/ and the root *.config.ts.\n// - tsconfig.tests.json: every *.test.ts, which may import anything.\n// A new directory under those roots joins its project by itself; a new root directory joins tsconfig.json's\n// \"include\" and one project's. A project reaches another's files only through \"references\" (tsc's TS6307 names a\n// file outside them): add the reference, never the file to a second project. Each project lists package-lock.json,\n// because tsc -b skips a project by its own files alone: a dependency change must rebuild it.\n{\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"references\": [\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.apps.json\" },\n    { \"path\": \"./tsconfig.tests.json\" }\n  ]\n}\n# Prettier checks code, data and the generated docs (ADR-0014, amendment 2). Hand-written prose stays as its author\n# wrote it: Prettier would re-pad its tables and rewrite its emphasis and lists, and DOCTRINE.md and docs/research/\n# are frozen. .gitignore's paths (out/, node_modules/, .cache/…) are skipped too.\n*.md\n!docs/INDEX.md\n!docs/API.md\n!docs/ERRORS.md\n!docs/escalations/README.md\ntests/baselines/port/\n# The clip sets: machine-written by tools/anim/repack.ts, each clip its codec text() (three lines a key), pinned\n# byte for byte by tests/unit/data/anim/sets/; Prettier would spread each key over 13 lines (ADR-0010 amendment 2).\ndata/anim/sets/\n# Written by npm.\npackage-lock.json\n# The lean package: the engine built as one module, and its page and README, hand-written but for the blocks\n# tools/lib/lean.ts writes (ADR-0024 amendment 1).\nlean/\n# The one-file playground: a build, written by node x html --write (tools/lib/oneFile.ts, ADR-0023 amendment 5).\nplayground.html\nignored\nsfx:blip sfx:bodyFall sfx:boom sfx:boxDeath sfx:boxHit sfx:boxLaunch sfx:boxStep sfx:boxStepIron sfx:boxThud sfx:boxTorch sfx:bump sfx:cancel sfx:charge sfx:climbGrip sfx:coin sfx:confirm sfx:crouchCloth sfx:die sfx:door sfx:doorBreak sfx:doorClose sfx:doorLocked sfx:doorOpen sfx:drawGun sfx:drumCrash sfx:drumHat sfx:drumKick sfx:drumOpenHat sfx:drumSnare sfx:drumTom sfx:dryFire sfx:explode sfx:glassBreak sfx:grab sfx:heal sfx:hit sfx:holsterGun sfx:hurt sfx:impactBody sfx:impactConcrete sfx:impactDirt sfx:impactGlass sfx:impactMetal sfx:impactWood sfx:jump sfx:jump2 sfx:key sfx:kick sfx:kickHit sfx:ladderRung sfx:land sfx:landBody sfx:laser sfx:launch sfx:mantle sfx:oneup sfx:pause sfx:pickup sfx:pistolShot sfx:powerup sfx:punch sfx:punchHit sfx:reload sfx:rifleShot sfx:secret sfx:select sfx:shoot sfx:slide sfx:step sfx:stepCarpet sfx:stepConcrete sfx:stepGrass sfx:stepGravel sfx:stepMetal sfx:stepTile sfx:stepWood sfx:stomp sfx:swing sfx:swish sfx:switchClick sfx:text sfx:warp sfx:whoosh sfx:wind sfx:windowSlide sfx:zipAttach sfx:zipRun\n71:      plugins: { jsdoc, 'hard-cap': families.family('hard-cap', 'max-lines') },\n74:        'max-lines': ['warn', { max: 400 }],\n75:        'hard-cap/max-lines': ['error', { max: 600 }],","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"a1c2b6b0-65dd-4c0b-80a0-2922d4b77495","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:22:12.716Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// T0 project: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: the labs, the fixtures, the tools, the test pages,\n// specs and helpers, the Claude Code hooks and the root configs (tsconfig.check.json).\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"composite\": true,\n    \"emitDeclarationOnly\": true,\n    \"rootDir\": \".\",\n    \"outDir\": \"node_modules/.cache/tsc\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"labs\", \"fixtures\", \"tools\", \"tests\", \".claude/hooks\", \"*.config.ts\", \"package-lock.json\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"**/*.test.ts\"],\n  \"references\": [{ \"path\": \"./tsconfig.engine.json\" }]\n}\n// T0's type check (`npm run typecheck`, inside `npm run check`): `tsc -b` over three composite projects that emit\n// declarations only, into node_modules/.cache/tsc/. A run skips a project whose own files and upstream declarations\n// did not change, and re-checks only what a change can reach (ADR-0014, amendment 7). Together the projects hold\n// exactly tsconfig.json's files, each once (tools/checkAll.test.ts checks it):\n// - tsconfig.engine.json: engine/, without its tests. The engine imports nothing outside it (PLAN.md §6.1).\n// - tsconfig.apps.json: the code that runs on the engine, without its tests: labs/, fixtures/, tools/, tests/ (pages,\n//   specs, setup