{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FbGtsUfTYmLpBEgYnxitq1","type":"tool_result","content":"2: * @file The first sixteen filters' fields (PLAN.md WP 7.4, WP 11.5; WP 13.31 adds to `grade` and `outline`): the\n3- * shading's (`ao`, `gi`, `ssr`, `air`), `bloom` and `aa`, which run before the composite and take only `off` or `all`,\n4: * and the composite's own (`cel`, `pixel`, `palette`, `outline`, `stylize`, `grade`, `scanlines`, `grain`, `chroma`,\n5- * `screen`). engine/gfx/post/filters.ts says what each does in the picture and in which order; the filters Style Lab\n6- * brought are engine/gfx/post/filterFieldsMore.ts's. Sizes are in the picture's own pixels, unless a field says\n7- * \"at 1080 lines\".\n8- *\n9- * WP 13.31 adds Style Lab's further grade (michaelcrosato/my-ai-3d-demo@34c6fa1, src/runtime/registry/grade.js:\n10- * lift, gamma, vibrance, hue, sepia, bleach bypass) and line options (src/runtime/registry/lines.js: distance fade,\n11- * wobble and boil), each defaulting to the value that leaves the picture as it was.\n12- *\n13- * Invariants: every number has its range; every new field's default changes nothing, so a look written before them\n14- * draws as it did.\n15- *\n16- * @example\n17- * CORE_FILTER_FIELDS.grade.properties.hue.default; // 0\n18- * @see engine/gfx/post/filters.test.ts\n--\n86:    outline: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'A dark one-block rim outside pixel-art silhouettes.' },\n87-    snap: {\n88-      type: 'boolean',\n89-      default: true,\n90-      description: 'Snap the camera to the block grid while the environment is pixel art, so it does not shimmer.',\n91-    },\n92-    smooth: {\n93-      type: 'boolean',\n94-      default: false,\n95-      description:\n96-        \"Carry the snapped camera's sub-block remainder as a smooth offset of the whole picture on the page (its canvas needs a margin of two drawn pixels, `--my3dge-pixel` each).\",\n97-    },\n98-  }),\n99-  palette: filter('Colour reduction: levels per channel or a fixed palette, with ordered (Bayer) dithering.', {\n100-    scope: scope(),\n--\n105:  outline: filter('Outlines where depth jumps, surfaces crease or outline groups meet.', {\n106-    scope: scope(),\ncommon.ts\ndisplay.ts\nedges.ts\nlens.ts\nmedia.ts\nstylize.ts\ntone.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"d9f09801-7dee-4ac0-b8be-0aa2bf981957","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:37:59.726Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2: * @file The first sixteen filters' fields (PLAN.md WP 7.4, WP 11.5; WP 13.31 adds to `grade` and `outline`): the\n3- * shading's (`ao`, `gi`, `ssr`, `air`), `bloom` and `aa`, which run before the composite and take only `off` or `all`,\n4: * and the composite's own (`cel`, `pixel`, `palette`, `outline`, `stylize`, `grade`, `scanlines`, `grain`, `chroma`,\n5- * `screen`). engine/gfx/post/filters.ts says what each does in the picture and in which order; the filters Style Lab\n6- * brought are engine/gfx/post/filterFieldsMore.ts's. Sizes are in the picture's own pixels, unless a field says\n7- * \"at 1080 lines\".\n8- *\n9- * WP 13.31 adds Style Lab's further grade (michaelcrosato/my-ai-3d-demo@34c6fa1, src/runtime/registry/grade.js:\n10- * lift, gamma, vibrance, hue, sepia, bleach bypass) and line options (src/runtime/registry/lines.js: distance fade,\n11- * wobble and boil), each defaulting to the value that leaves the picture as it was.\n12- *\n13- * Invariants: every number has its range; every new field's default changes nothing, so a look written before them\n14- * draws as it did.\n15- *\n16- * @example\n17- * CORE_FILTER_FIELDS.grade.properties.hue.default; // 0\n18- * @see engine/gfx/post/filters.test.ts\n--\n86:    outline: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: 'A dark one-block rim outside pixel-art silhouettes.' },\n87-    snap: {\n88-      type: 'boolean',\n89-      default: true,\n90-      description: 'Snap the camera to the block grid while the environment is pixel art, so it does not shimmer.',\n91-    },\n92-    smooth: {\n93-      type: 'boolean',\n94-      default: false,\n95-      description:\n96-        \"Carry the snapped camera's sub-block remainder as a smooth offset of the whole picture on the page (its canvas needs a margin of two drawn pixels, `--my3dge-pixel` each).\",\n97-    },\n98-  }),\n99-  palette: filter('Colour reduction: levels per channel or a fixed palette, with ordered (Bayer) dithering.', {\n100-    scope: scope(),\n--\n105:  outline: filter('Outlines where depth jumps, surfaces crease or outline groups meet.', {\n106-    scope: scope(),\ncommon.ts\ndisplay.ts\nedges.ts\nlens.ts\nmedia.ts\nstylize.ts\ntone.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FbGtsUfTYmLpBEgYnxitq1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
