ement would name the field.\n5. **`input.lastDevice` did not follow the mouse on hover or click in my tests,** so I tracked the device from the page's\n   own events. A note in its doc on when it changes would help.\n6. **Library ids clash without warning until load:** `prop:bench`, `sfx:whoosh`, `sfx:kick`. `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` is clear,\n   but only at page load; `npm run check` passes. Reserving a game prefix, or checking in `x check`, would catch it sooner.\n7. **JSON imports fail the type check (TS6307)** though lint and Node accept them, and `tsconfig.*` is locked. I keep the\n   borrowed clips as a string constant parsed at load. A level-of-effort note in the guide would have saved the detour.\n8. **The guide's `labs/playground/...` paths are not in a game's workspace,** as the plan warned.\n9. **`erasableSyntaxOnly` refuses TypeScript parameter properties.** Fine, but it surfaces only at `tsc -b`, not in Vite's\n   build, so the page ran happily with code the check later refused.\n10. **`x shot`'s `LOOK_BLOWN` flags a pale sky** at 26%, for a look that means to be high-key. It is only advice, but there\n    is no way to accept it per look.\n\n## What worked well\n\nDeterminism across Node and Chromium held without any effort: replays agree first time. Headless `createHeadless` with\nscene actions made every activity testable by bot at step speed. The clip layer with hand-written strips scrubbed from\nthe sim was exactly as good as the plan said: a pose is one line of numbers, and it reads on screen.\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":12,"newStart":6,"newLines":53,"lines":[" "," ## Requests"," ","-<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->","+1. **Warm only the props a scene can spawn.** `createPropMeshes` makes a batch for every registered prop","+   (`engine/gfx/props.ts`: `options.props ?? registry.list('prop')`), and they all warm when the first prop arrives. On","+   SwiftShader a page with one prop spawned took 38 s with `gfx.warmUp=asked` and 89 s without; with none, 9 s. The AI Hub","+   allows 20 s. I expected a scene to warm what it uses. Instead the session scene spawns no prop at all, and imports only","+   its own scene's modules so the island's props are not registered. A `props: [...]` list on a scene, or warming a","+   prop's batches when its first instance arrives, would fix it.","+2. **Tint or colour an actor per instance.** A body's `slots` are a palette, but an actor can only name a whole body. Four","+   seat colours, six tracksuits and three looks became 48 `defineBody` calls in a loop. `spawnActor({ palette })`, read by","+   the view, would be one line.","+3. **A way to hide an actor or a prop without moving it.** \"Shown only while in the same area\" (hub ghosts) and \"hidden","+   until Day 4\" both became writing y = -30, with `placeActor`'s ceiling check to keep in mind.","+4. **A public `createRepeat`.** `engine/ui/widgets.ts` has the held-direction repeat every menu wants, but it is not in the","+   public API, so I wrote it again for a value-row panel.","+5. **A sea.** A huge flat prop as the plan describes shows dark mip-averaged banding near the horizon at grazing angles,","+   an edge where it ends, and a band below the horizon where nothing is drawn. A haze ring past the fog end and a softer","+   texture fixed it, after an hour. A `water` primitive that fades to the fog and has no edge would save every island."," "," ## Friction"," ","-<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->","+1. **Spawns inside `setup` and inside actions are queued to the boundary, and the failure is silent.** `w.spawn` returns an","+   id but `w.query` and `w.get` do not see it until the entry point ends. I looked people up by name in `setup`; every seat","+   got actor -1, and all poses silently did nothing. Tests passed, because scores do not need a body. It took a screenshot","+   to see. `w.get(id)` on a queued spawn could warn in a dev mode.","+2. **`inspector.describe('setting', path)` returns a list of `{ key, value, differs }`,** not the field's object. The plan","+   and the name suggest the object. My sliders wrote NaN (`CORE_BAD_SETTING`). A `field(path)` member would be clearer.","+3. **`defineActionMap` requires the four move actions** even for a menu map with nothing to move: `CORE_BAD_SPEC ... move","+   names \"forward\", which actions lacks`. Fine, but the message reads as if I named them.","+4. **`spawnProp` takes `{ prop, at, yaw }`.** The first guess `{ prop, position }` crashes in `propPose` with `Cannot read","+   properties of undefined (reading '0')`, far from the call. A checked placement would name the field.","+5. **`input.lastDevice` did not follow the mouse on hover or click in my tests,** so I tracked the device from the page's","+   own events. A note in its doc on when it changes would help.","+6. **Library ids clash without warning until load:** `prop:bench`, `sfx:whoosh`, `sfx:kick`. `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` is clear,","+   but only at page load; `npm run check` passes. Reserving a game prefix, or checking in `x check`, would catch it sooner.","+7. **JSON imports fail the type check (TS6307)** though lint and Node accept them, and `tsconfig.*` is locked. I keep the","+   borrowed clips as a string constant parsed at load. A level-of-effort note in the guide would have saved the detour.","+8. **The guide's `labs/playground/...` paths are not in a game's workspace,** as the plan warned.","+9. **`erasableSyntaxOnly` refuses TypeScript parameter properties.** Fine, but it surfaces only at `tsc -b`, not in Vite's","+   build, so the page ran happily with code the check later refused.","+10. **`x shot`'s `LOOK_BLOWN` flags a pale sky** at 26%, for a look that means to be high-key. It is only advice, but there","+    is no way to accept it per look."," ","+## What worked well","+","+Determinism across Node and Chromium held without any effort: replays agree first time. Headless `createHeadless` with","+scene actions made every activity testable by bot at step speed. The clip layer with hand-written strips scrubbed from","+the sim was exactly as good as the plan said: a pose is one line of numbers, and it reads on screen.","+"," ## Local engine patches"," "," <!--"]}],"originalFile":"# Engine feedback: teeter\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n## Friction\n\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EeGNTaa8rVYsByrdqLWnRM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
