{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjhXXES5T8KXjdTmEwD7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9923,"cache_read_input_tokens":797291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9923},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"69875b45-f94a-48a5-b21a-d09d0f8ff1ec","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:26:26.664Z","request_id":"req_011CgjhXWsbnZ7xHtX6DnQUF","thinking_duration_ms":8504,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjhXXES5T8KXjdTmEwD7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013SGBzG9fDDe53exPeVSZok","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='labs/game/materials/retreat.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  map: { texture: 'texture:tiles', seed: 3 },\"\"\",\"\"\"  map: { texture: 'texture:tiles', seed: 3, params: { tones: '#fbfdfe,#f1f5f7', glaze: '#ffffff', grout: '#d3dce1' } },\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"5. **`input.lastDevice` did not follow the mouse on hover or click in my tests,** so I tracked the device from the page's\\n   own events. A note in its doc on when it changes would help.\",\"5. **`input.lastDevice` stayed on the keyboard while the mouse hovered over a menu,** so I tracked the device from the\\n   page's own events. A note in its doc on when it changes would help.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='labs/game/ui/about-data.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"/** The feedback questions and answers, filled in before the final build. */\")\nb=s.index(\"/** The credits. */\")\ns=s[:a]+'''/** Testing feedback: the questions in TASK.md's order, with the answers. */\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK: readonly (readonly [string, string])[] = [\n  ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About 40 across the run, from wrong ids and lint to play-breaking bugs.'],\n  [\n    'How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?',\n    'Six: every class pose silently not playing (seats held no actor), a crash at the session scene start, a boot far past the hub deadline, the Programme restarting the first activity for ever, Gerald walking off the map after Island Jog, and a press opening and closing the same screen.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran?',\n    'The scripted playthrough of the whole game with the human-like bot, which proved no softlock on three seeds, and the page drive to the credits with one kind of input, which found the Programme loop the sim could not see.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran?',\n    \"The look metrics from the shot tool: it told me the pale sky was blown out, and never that a dark band sat on the horizon. A screenshot found that in a second.\",\n  ],\n];\n\n/** Engine feedback. */\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK: readonly (readonly [string, string])[] = [\n  [\n    'What did you like most about the engine?',\n    'Play is reproducible and needs no screen. Every activity could be played by bots on ten seeds at step speed, and replays matched in Node and Chromium first time. A pose as one line of numbers, scrubbed from the sim, was a joy.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?',\n    'Yes. Spawns inside setup are queued, so looking people up there silently gave every seat no body. I guessed wrong on the prop placement shape, on what describe returns, and on three library ids. The horizon took an hour.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?',\n    'The Wobble Model and the activity framework that makes eleven activities and a finale one shape, with bots; then the whole 10-foot front end: panels, Balance Disc, glyphs, Dev Mode, attract and the hub card.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine?',\n    \"Warm-up: the engine builds every registered prop's pipelines when the first prop arrives, which on a software GPU is past the hub's deadline, so a session scene has to draw its pavilion with no props at all.\",\n  ],\n  ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'none'],\n  [\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?',\n    'Warm only the props a scene can spawn.',\n  ],\n];\n\n/** Prompt feedback. */\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK: readonly (readonly [string, string])[] = [\n  [\n    'What did you like most about this prompt?',\n    'The plan marks what was tested and gives real numbers, such as the sway rate that makes a thumb better than doing nothing. Its bots for judging feel were the right answer to nobody being able to play.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was confusing?',\n    'The plan was tested on an older engine commit and client hash than I got, so some traps had moved. Its one-line size limits and \"two short sentences\" sit beside seed lines of five sentences.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the hardest thing to do?',\n    'Judging feel and looks with no person and no real GPU: every sound by numbers, every picture on a software renderer at a few frames a second, and a 45-minute game to hold in one head.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What would you change in this prompt?',\n    'Pin the engine commit and client version the plan was tested on, and give a boot-time budget for the island as well as the session, since warm-up cost drives how props should be made from the start.',\n  ],\n];\n\n'''+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs <<'EOF'\n/**\n * @file Writes exit-interview.json from labs/game/ui/about-data.ts, so the About screen, the chat reply and the interview\n * agree (PLAN.md section 19). Usage, from the dev folder: node labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs <output.json>\n */\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\n\nconst about = await import(pathToFileURL(resolve('labs/game/ui/about-data.ts')).href);\nconst answers = (list) => list.map(([, answer]) => answer);\nconst interview = {\n  sourceInformation: { ...about.SOURCE_INFO },\n  testingFeedback: answers(about.TESTING_FEEDBACK),\n  engineFeedback: answers(about.ENGINE_FEEDBACK),\n  promptFeedback: answers(about.PROMPT_FEEDBACK),\n  aiHub: {\n    name: 'Teeter Fit',\n    tagline: 'Stand still. It is harder than it looks.',\n    description:\n      'A deadpan wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock. Eleven balance activities, one verb, a Wobble Age, and a storm where your thumb holds the island level.',\n    type: 'Game',\n    genre: 'Sports',\n    source: 'Wii Fit',\n    series: '',\n    players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both',\n    tags: ['3d', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'arcade', 'sports', 'story'],\n  },\n};\nconst text = `${JSON.stringify(interview, null, 2)}\\n`;\nJSON.parse(text);\nwriteFileSync(process.argv[2], text);\nEOF\nnode labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs ../exit-interview.json 2>&1 | tail -2 | cut -c1-200; python3 -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d.keys()), list(d['sourceInformation'].keys()), len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']))\"; tail -3 out/vitest-all.log | cut -c1-200","description":"Fill feedback answers and write the exit interview","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9923,"cache_read_input_tokens":797291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9923},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"b40e8598-2043-4dcf-b02e-cce1351f9381","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:26:48.252Z","request_id":"req_011CgjhXWsbnZ7xHtX6DnQUF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013SGBzG9fDDe53exPeVSZok":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='labs/game/materials/retreat.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  map: { texture: 'texture:tiles', seed: 3 },\"\"\",\"\"\"  map: { texture: 'texture:tiles', seed: 3, params: { tones: '#fbfdfe,#f1f5f7', glaze: '#ffffff', grout: '#d3dce1' } },\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"5. **`input.lastDevice` did not follow the mouse on hover or click in my tests,** so I tracked the device from the page's\\n   own events. A note in its doc on when it changes would help.\",\"5. **`input.lastDevice` stayed on the keyboard while the mouse hovered over a menu,** so I tracked the device from the\\n   page's own events. A note in its doc on when it changes would help.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='labs/game/ui/about-data.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"/** The feedback questions and answers, filled in before the final build. */\")\nb=s.index(\"/** The credits. */\")\ns=s[:a]+'''/** Testing feedback: the questions in TASK.md's order, with the answers. */\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK: readonly (readonly [string, string])[] = [\n  ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About 40 across the run, from wrong ids and lint to play-breaking bugs.'],\n  [\n    'How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?',\n    'Six: every class pose silently not playing (seats held no actor), a crash at the session scene start, a boot far past the hub deadline, the Programme restarting the first activity for ever, Gerald walking off the map after Island Jog, and a press opening and closing the same screen.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the most helpful test you ran?',\n    'The scripted playthrough of the whole game with the human-like bot, which proved no softlock on three seeds, and the page drive to the credits with one kind of input, which found the Programme loop the sim could not see.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the least helpful test you ran?',\n    \"The look metrics from the shot tool: it told me the pale sky was blown out, and never that a dark band sat on the horizon. A screenshot found that in a second.\",\n  ],\n];\n\n/** Engine feedback. */\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK: readonly (readonly [string, string])[] = [\n  [\n    'What did you like most about the engine?',\n    'Play is reproducible and needs no screen. Every activity could be played by bots on ten seeds at step speed, and replays matched in Node and Chromium first time. A pose as one line of numbers, scrubbed from the sim, was a joy.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?',\n    'Yes. Spawns inside setup are queued, so looking people up there silently gave every seat no body. I guessed wrong on the prop placement shape, on what describe returns, and on three library ids. The horizon took an hour.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?',\n    'The Wobble Model and the activity framework that makes eleven activities and a finale one shape, with bots; then the whole 10-foot front end: panels, Balance Disc, glyphs, Dev Mode, attract and the hub card.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the hardest part about using the engine?',\n    \"Warm-up: the engine builds every registered prop's pipelines when the first prop arrives, which on a software GPU is past the hub's deadline, so a session scene has to draw its pavilion with no props at all.\",\n  ],\n  ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'none'],\n  [\n    'If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?',\n    'Warm only the props a scene can spawn.',\n  ],\n];\n\n/** Prompt feedback. */\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK: readonly (readonly [string, string])[] = [\n  [\n    'What did you like most about this prompt?',\n    'The plan marks what was tested and gives real numbers, such as the sway rate that makes a thumb better than doing nothing. Its bots for judging feel were the right answer to nobody being able to play.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was confusing?',\n    'The plan was tested on an older engine commit and client hash than I got, so some traps had moved. Its one-line size limits and \"two short sentences\" sit beside seed lines of five sentences.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What was the hardest thing to do?',\n    'Judging feel and looks with no person and no real GPU: every sound by numbers, every picture on a software renderer at a few frames a second, and a 45-minute game to hold in one head.',\n  ],\n  [\n    'What would you change in this prompt?',\n    'Pin the engine commit and client version the plan was tested on, and give a boot-time budget for the island as well as the session, since warm-up cost drives how props should be made from the start.',\n  ],\n];\n\n'''+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs <<'EOF'\n/**\n * @file Writes exit-interview.json from labs/game/ui/about-data.ts, so the About screen, the chat reply and the interview\n * agree (PLAN.md section 19). Usage, from the dev folder: node labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs <output.json>\n */\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\n\nconst about = await import(pathToFileURL(resolve('labs/game/ui/about-data.ts')).href);\nconst answers = (list) => list.map(([, answer]) => answer);\nconst interview = {\n  sourceInformation: { ...about.SOURCE_INFO },\n  testingFeedback: answers(about.TESTING_FEEDBACK),\n  engineFeedback: answers(about.ENGINE_FEEDBACK),\n  promptFeedback: answers(about.PROMPT_FEEDBACK),\n  aiHub: {\n    name: 'Teeter Fit',\n    tagline: 'Stand still. It is harder than it looks.',\n    description:\n      'A deadpan wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock. Eleven balance activities, one verb, a Wobble Age, and a storm where your thumb holds the island level.',\n    type: 'Game',\n    genre: 'Sports',\n    source: 'Wii Fit',\n    series: '',\n    players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both',\n    tags: ['3d', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'arcade', 'sports', 'story'],\n  },\n};\nconst text = `${JSON.stringify(interview, null, 2)}\\n`;\nJSON.parse(text);\nwriteFileSync(process.argv[2], text);\nEOF\nnode labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs ../exit-interview.json 2>&1 | tail -2 | cut -c1-200; python3 -c \"\nimport