m -rf out; ls | head -30 | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; grep -n \"lines\\|prompt\\|What was\" /dev/null; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'))\nfor k,v in d['sourceInformation'].items(): print(k,':',v)\nfor k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']:\n    print(k)\n    for a in d[k]: print(' -',a)\nprint(d['aiHub'])\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/PROGRESS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"## Status\")\nb=s.index(\"## Test tally\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"## Status (done)\n- verify: 25 passed, 0 failed. npm test passes. Final HTML and exit-interview.json are in work/ root; the HTML matches the verified build byte for byte.\n- Only the chat reply was left.\n\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Confirm tests, clean generated output, print the reports"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KMeDPQjxMPqCqEDr86LHz7","type":"tool_result","content":" Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  40 passed (40)\nexit 0\nAGENTS.md CLAUDE.md DOCTRINE.md ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md GEMINI.md README.md data docs engine engine-lock.json eslint.config.js index.html labs node_modules package-lock.json package.json scripts tests tools tsconfig.apps.json tsconfig.base.json tsconfig.check.json tsconfig.engine.json tsconfig.json tsconfig.tests.json vite.config.ts x.js \ndate : 2026-11-05 01:56:01\nsource : Wii Fit\nplan : PLAN.md\ngenre : A 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities round a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual meta game and a comedy story\nperspective : Third person: a chase camera on the island and a purpose-built camera for each activity\ntech : my-3dge at 2dbd829 (full workspace, engine read-only), three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7, TypeScript 5.9; HTML/CSS UI\nartDirection : The engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets: a clean, high-key brochure island\nanimation : The engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim, so your thumb is the exercise\naudio : Tracker songs, defineSfx effects, Animalese-style gibberish syllable voices, all code, no audio files, music at 10% by default\nonline : AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, up to 4; same-screen Group Class on its own, up to 4 pads\ntesting : Headless scripts allowed: bots on 10 seeds per activity, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, browser checks in Playwright, sparing screenshots; no review subagents\nresearch : The AI Hub protocol README and the my-3dge guide; nothing else was needed beyond the plan\nenvironment : Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\nmodel : Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\nusage : added on import\ntestingFeedback\n - About 45 across the run, from wrong ids and lint to play-breaking bugs.\n - Nine: every class pose silently not playing (seats held no actor), a crash at the session scene start, a boot far past the hub deadline, the Programme restarting the first activity for ever, Gerald walking off the map after Island Jog, a press opening and closing the same screen, a frame crash in Pose Class, a crash removing the diving judges in mid-step, and the Carry on press dropping you straight back into the activity.\n - The scripted playthrough of the whole game with the human-like bot, which proved no softlock on three seeds and found the mid-step crash, and the page drive to the credits with one kind of input, which found the Programme loop and the Carry on bug that the sim could not see.\n - The look metrics from the shot tool: it told me the pale sky was blown out, and never that a dark band sat on the horizon. A screenshot found that in a second.\nengineFeedback\n - Play is reproducible and needs no screen. Every activity could be played by bots on ten seeds at step speed, and replays matched in Node and Chromium first time. A pose as one line of numbers, scrubbed from the sim, was a joy.\n - Yes. Spawns inside setup are queued, so looking people up there silently gave every seat no body. I guessed wrong on the prop placement shape, on what describe returns, and on three library ids. The horizon took an hour.\n - The Wobble Model and the activity framework that makes eleven activities and a finale one shape, with bots; then the whole 10-foot front end: panels, Balance Disc, glyphs, Dev Mode, attract and the hub card.\n - Warm-up: the engine builds every registered prop's pipelines when the first prop arrives, which on a software GPU is past the hub's deadline, so a session scene has to draw its pavilion with no props at all.\n - none\n - Warm only the props a scene can spawn.\npromptFeedback\n - The plan marks what was tested and gives real numbers, such as the sway rate that makes a thumb better than doing nothing. Its bots for judging feel were the right answer to nobody being able to play.\n - The plan was tested on an older engine commit and client hash than I got, so some of its details had moved. Its rule of two short sentences a line sits beside seed lines of five.\n - Judging feel and looks with no person and no real GPU: every sound by numbers, every picture on a software renderer at a few frames a second, and a 45-minute game to hold in one head.\n - Pin the engine commit and client version the plan was tested on, and give a boot-time budget for the island as well as the session, since warm-up cost drives how props should be made from the start.\n{'name': 'Teeter Fit', 'tagline': 'Stand still. It is harder than it looks.', 'description': 'A deadpan wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock. Eleven balance activities, one verb, a Wobble Age, and a storm where your thumb holds the island level.', 'type': 'Game', 'genre': 'Sports', 'source': 'Wii Fit', 'series': '', 'players': '1–4', 'controls': 'Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both', 'tags': ['3d', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'arcade', 'sports', 'story']}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"dafb17bd-7920-4d40-8502-10c69262e301","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:56:41.493Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" Test Files  3 passed (3)\n      Tests  40 passed (40)\nexit 0\nAGENTS.md CLAUDE.md DOCTRINE.md ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md GEMINI.md README.md data docs engine engine-lock.json eslint.config.js index.html labs node_modules package-lock.json package.json scripts tests tools tsconfig.apps.json tsconfig.base.json tsconfig.check.json tsconfig.engine.json tsconfig.json tsconfig.tests.json vite.config.ts x.js \ndate : 2026-11-05 01:56:01\nsource : Wii Fit\nplan : PLAN.md\ngenre : A 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities round a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual meta game and a comedy story\nperspective : Third person: a chase camera on the island and a purpose-built camera for each activity\ntech : my-3dge at 2dbd829 (full workspace, engine read-only), three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7, TypeScript 5.9; HTML/CSS UI\nartDirection : The engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets: a clean, high-key brochure island\nanimation : The engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim, so your thumb is the exercise\naudio : Tracker songs, defineSfx effects, Animalese-style gibberish syllable voices, all code, no audio files, music at 10% by default\nonline : AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, up to 4; same-screen Group Class on its own, up to 4 pads\ntesting : Headless scripts allowed: bots on 10 seeds per activity, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, browser checks in Playwright, sparing screenshots; no review subagents\nresearch : The AI Hub protocol README and the my-3dge guide; nothing else was needed beyond the plan\nenvironment : Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\nmodel : Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\nusage : added on import\ntestingFeedback\n - About 45 across the run, from wrong ids and lint to play-breaking bugs.\n - Nine: every class pose silently not playing (seats held no actor), a crash at the session scene start, a boot far past the hub deadline, the Programme restarting the first activity for ever, Gerald walking off the map after Island Jog, a press opening and closing the same screen, a frame crash in Pose Class, a crash removing the diving judges in mid-step, and the Carry on press dropping you straight back into the activity.\n - The scripted playthrough of the whole game with the human-like bot, which proved no softlock on three seeds and found the mid-step crash, and the page drive to the credits with one kind of input, which found the Programme loop and the Carry on bug that the sim could not see.\n - The look metrics from the shot tool: it told me the pale sky was blown out, and never that a dark band sat on the horizon. A screenshot found that in a second.\nengineFeedback\n - Play is reproducible and needs no screen. Every activity could be played by bots on ten seeds at step speed, and replays matched in Node and Chromium first time. A pose as one line of numbers, scrubbed from the sim, was a joy.\n - Yes. Spawns inside setup are queued, so looking people up there silently gave every seat no body. I guessed wrong on the prop placement shape, on what describe returns, and on three library ids. The horizon took an hour.\n - The Wobble Model and the activity framework that makes eleven activities and a finale one shape, with bots; then the whole 10-foot front end: panels, Balance Disc, glyphs, Dev Mode, attract and the hub card.\n - Warm-up: the engine builds every registered prop's pipelines when the first prop arrives, which on a software GPU is past the hub's deadline, so a session scene has to draw its pavilion with no props at all.\n - none\n - Warm only the props a scene can spawn.\npromptFeedback\n - The plan marks what was tested and gives real numbers, such as the sway rate that makes a thumb better than doing nothing. Its bots for judging feel were the right answer to nobody being able to play.\n - The plan was tested on an older engine commit and client hash than I got, so some of its details had moved. Its rule of two short sentences a line sits beside seed lines of five.\n - Judging feel and looks with no person and no real GPU: every sound by numbers, every picture on a software renderer at a few frames a second, and a 45-minute game to hold in one head.\n - Pin the engine commit and client version the plan was tested on, and give a boot-time budget for the island as well as the session, since warm-up cost drives how props should be made from the start.\n{'name': 'Teeter Fit', 'tagline': 'Stand still. It is harder than it looks.', 'description': 'A deadpan wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock. Eleven balance activities, one verb, a Wobble Age, and a storm where your thumb holds the island level.', 'type': 'Game', 'genre': 'Sports', 'source': 'Wii Fit', 'series': '', 'players': '1–4', 'controls': 'Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both', 'tags': ['3d', 'third-person', 'comedy', 'arcade', 'sports', 'story']}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KMeDPQjxMPqCqEDr86LHz7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
