{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkDJFAujnzVfCjyiuDBV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Teeter Fit is finished**, and it's in the folder as a single HTML file that runs from `file://` and fetches nothing. The final `verify.mjs` run reports 25 passed, 0 failed, and `npm test` passes. The HTML is byte-identical to the build verify tested.\n\nYou play a guest at a wellness retreat run by a retired bathroom scale, on an island balanced on one rock. It has five days of balance activities, all played by leaning your weight. It ends with a storm where your thumb holds the whole island level.\n\n## What the tests can't tell you\n- **Nobody has played it by hand.** Feel was judged only by bots that imitate a delayed human thumb. Hoop Patrol and Island Jog scored 1000 for all three active bots, so those two may be easier than the numbers suggest.\n- **Hardware stand-ins:**\n  - All rendering was on a software GPU, at a few frames a second.\n  - The controller was a stub, and sound was checked by numbers only.\n  - Mouse lean was tested with synthetic events, because headless Chromium reports no movement under pointer lock.\n- **Boot time on a real GPU is unmeasured.** On the software renderer the island took about 30 s with `gfx.warmUp=asked`, which every test used; without it, a page with props took about 90 s. A hub session takes about 10 s.\n- **Machine memory:** verify retries a stage when the shared machine's memory kills a worker or browser, because earlier runs failed that way with no game fault. Every stage passes in the final run.\n\n## Where I departed from the plan\nThese are also noted in the game's `labs/game/README.md`.\n- **Camera:** one data-driven shot camera instead of one camera mode per activity.\n- **Hub sessions:** they spawn no props, because warming them overran the hub's 20 s limit. The pavilion there is telegraphs and stacked blocks.\n- **Gull and Frog:** small actors instead of blob rigs, because the engine's blobs can only be pink.\n- **Menus:** one custom panel widget instead of `createMenu`, because Settings needs value rows and paging.\n- **Clips:** I only borrowed CC0 clips.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 01:56:01\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities round a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual meta game and a comedy story. Third person: a chase camera on the island and a purpose-built camera for each activity.\n- **Tech:** my-3dge at 2dbd829 (full workspace, engine read-only), three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7, TypeScript 5.9; HTML/CSS UI\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets: a clean, high-key brochure island\n- **Animation:** the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim, so your thumb is the exercise\n- **Audio:** tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, Animalese-style gibberish syllable voices, all code, no audio files, music at 10% by default\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, up to 4; same-screen Group Class on its own, up to 4 pads\n- **Testing:** headless scripts allowed: bots on 10 seeds per activity, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, browser checks in Playwright, sparing screenshots; no review subagents\n- **Research:** the AI Hub protocol README and the my-3dge guide; nothing else was needed beyond the plan\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 45 across the run, from wrong ids and lint to play-breaking bugs.\n- **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** Nine:\n  - every class pose silently not playing (seats held no actor)\n  - a crash at the session scene start\n  - a boot far past the hub deadline\n  - the Programme restarting the first activity for ever\n  - Gerald walking off the map after Island Jog\n  - a press opening and closing the same screen\n  - a frame crash in Pose Class\n  - a crash removing the diving judges in mid-step\n  - the Carry on press dropping you straight back into the activity\n- **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted playthrough of the whole game with the human-like bot, which proved no softlock on three seeds and found the mid-step crash. Also the page drive to the credits with one kind of input, which found the Programme loop and the Carry on bug that the sim could not see.\n- **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The look metrics from the shot tool: it told me the pale sky was blown out, and never that a dark band sat on the horizon. A screenshot found that in a second.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** Play is reproducible and needs no screen. Every activity could be played by bots on ten seeds at step speed, and replays matched in Node and Chromium first time. A pose as one line of numbers, scrubbed from the sim, was a joy.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Spawns inside setup are queued, so looking people up there silently gave every seat no body. I guessed wrong on the prop placement shape, on what describe returns, and on three library ids. The horizon took an hour.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The Wobble Model and the activity framework that makes eleven activities and a finale one shape, with bots; then the whole 10-foot front end: panels, Balance Disc, glyphs, Dev Mode, attract and the hub card.\n- **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Warm-up: the engine builds every registered prop's pipelines when the first prop arrives, which on a software GPU is past the hub's deadline, so a session scene has to draw its pavilion with no props at all.\n- **What did you change in the engine, and why?** None.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Warm only the props a scene can spawn.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** The plan marks what was tested and gives real numbers, such as the sway rate that makes a thumb better than doing nothing. Its bots for judging feel were the right answer to nobody being able to play.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan was tested on an older engine commit and client hash than I got, so some of its details had moved. Its rule of two short sentences a line sits beside seed lines of five.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Judging feel and looks with no person and no real GPU: every sound by numbers, every picture on a software renderer at a few frames a second, and a 45-minute game to hold in one head.\n- **What would you change in this prompt?** Pin the engine commit and client version the plan was tested on, and give a boot-time budget for the island as well as the session, since warm-up cost drives how props should be made from the start.\n\n## Files\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601/` (dev folder; start with `labs/game/README.md` and `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2374,"cache_read_input_tokens":950558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2374},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"ab32a21c-bf96-4fc7-91a9-dba4cc0bebcc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:57:06.524Z","request_id":"req_011CgkDJEiPGcnNcYdHUMmTQ"}
