{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkDTFRYaTLUzpYAsSwRk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked the folder directly against `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` and the plan's Done list. Everything that can be done on this computer is done, and everything to hand in is there. That check also found one real miss, now fixed.\n\n**The fix:** the rolling credits said \"inspired by Wii Fit\", but the plan allows that word only on the About screen's Source line and in the hub's source field. Those are now the only two places it appears.\n\nThis changed one line of text after the last full verify, so the HTML no longer matches the verified build byte for byte. I rebuilt it and reran `npm run check` and the browser stages for boot, About and standalone: 53 passed, 0 failed.\n\n## Checked against the folder\n| Requirement | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `STAGE.md`: build the game, keep progress in `PROGRESS.md` | Done; `PROGRESS.md` is asked for there, not in `TASK.md` |\n| `TASK.md`: HTML in the root with the required name | Present, 7.1 MB, opens from `file://` |\n| `TASK.md`: dev files in the named subfolder | Present |\n| `TASK.md`: `exit-interview.json` | Parses, keys in the exact order asked, 4/6/4 feedback answers, no empty Source Information values |\n| `TASK.md`: Source Information and feedback on the About screen | Every value from the interview is in the build, and the browser check confirms every field and question shows on screen |\n| `TASK.md`: Source Information and feedback in the chat reply | In my previous message |\n| Plan: engine unchanged | `node x engine` reports 2135 files as shipped |\n| Plan: no TODOs or stubs | The only match is the search pattern inside `verify.mjs` |\n| Plan: hub client untouched | Byte-identical, SHA-256 starts `6ab6be43` |\n| Plan: `verify` and `npm test` | 25 passed, 0 failed, and 40 tests passed, both before the credits edit |\n\n## Why some things remain unmeasured\nHand-played feel and boot time on a real GPU can't be measured here. `TASK.md`'s \"What this computer doesn't have\" section says those are checked as far as possible with stand-ins and are never required. The stand-ins used were the bots, a stubbed pad, Playwright's touch profiles, audio judged by numbers, and two browser frames for multiplayer."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1913,"cache_read_input_tokens":958669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1913},"output_tokens":737,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"df1448d8-a597-4937-a1d4-6c0fb0299d29","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:58:51.854Z","request_id":"req_011CgkDTEjcwBZCTtfp8ympm"}
