{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mx3DFb3USTG7U9MkweLA49","type":"tool_result","content":"--- TASK.md on what this computer lacks\n26:Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n50:No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n52:- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n54:- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n55:- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n57:- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n--- PLAN.md on hand play and performance\n146:the human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep the sway slow. Nobody can play by\n147:hand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\n631:pavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\n948:| Fast sway | Doing nothing beats a human thumb **[tested]** | Keep `game.wobble.noiseRate` slow; judge with the delayed-thumb bot |\n960:- **Four players stand in for a human, since nobody here can play by hand.** All are bots writing seat input: *perfect* (no delay, gain 3); *human-like* (reads the CoB 250 ms late, gain 1.2, jitter 0.04); *sloppy* (350 ms, gai\n1049:| Performance out of scope | 9 (one protocol deadline only) |\n--- TASK.md hand-in lines\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included \n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"6bc1d340-460e-4fb2-9d91-2f1cbe25649b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:59:03.039Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"--- TASK.md on what this computer lacks\n26:Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n50:No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n52:- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n54:- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n55:- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n57:- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n--- PLAN.md on hand play and performance\n146:the human thumb,** because a 250 ms reaction turns correction into amplification, so keep t