{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Monitor, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user ran `/goal`: **\"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"** A session-scoped Stop hook blocks stopping until that condition holds.\n   - `STAGE.md`: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - `TASK.md` hand-ins:\n     - Line 11: single HTML `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601].html`.\n     - Line 24: dev subfolder of the same name; HTML in root.\n     - Line 93: \"CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen.\"\n     - Line 109: `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, in the exact shape.\n   - Constraints that remain in effect:\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server, bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks... Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n     - Tests go behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count.\n     - Keep one or two browsers open at once; keep every file inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent; don't run `playwright install`.\n     - Plan: engine read-only; do not `git init`, commit or restore in the dev folder; don't run `scripts/setup.sh`; the word \"Wii\" appears only on the About screen's Source line and the hub's source field; never weight/BMI/calorie talk.\n     - Commit only if asked (never asked).\n     - Use they/them for people whose pronouns aren't stated.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3dge engine at 2dbd829 (plan was tested on e7a1243): TypeScript, three.js r182 WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7; deterministic sim at 60 Hz; `createHeadless`; replays with goldens (Node + Chromium agree); scene `actions`; `defineScene/defineProp/defineBody/defineBuild/defineClipSet/defineTelegraph/defineEmitter/defineSfx/defineSong/defineLook/defineSky/defineCamera/defineActionMap`.\n   - One-scene rule: `game:island` (whole game) and `game:round` (hub session, spawns NO props). `main.ts` dynamically imports only the needed scene.\n   - Wobble Model (CoB in unit disc, slew, gain, instability, sway, breath/sync/calm), four bot players (perfect, human, sloppy, idle) plus mash.\n   - Pilot rule (all actors `player:false`); clip strips scrubbed by writing `clips.state.slots[i].t`; held people use a neutral `Stand` strip because per-step `placeActor` reads as falling.\n   - Single data-driven `cam3=shot` camera aimed by the `ui/shots.ts` table; `cam3=chase` for walking.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode; client 1.4.0 kept byte-identical (`session-client.txt`, SHA-256 `6ab6be43898e2db069bc21a94757d77d9c3f2a0cb76f01186490d3bd88d8717a`); watchdog ready at 14 s; own HTML card on its own rAF loop.\n   - Shared machine: earlyoom kills browsers when memory runs out; browser.py and hubcheck.py wait for memory and retry; verify retries memory-killed workers and the replay stage once.\n   - Run browser commands with `export CHROMIUM_PATH=$HOME/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell`.\n   - **Bash `cd` persists between calls: session cwd is now `work/`, so use absolute paths or an explicit `cd` in the same command.**\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   Root: `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/`\n   - `TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601.html`: final deliverable, 7.1 MB, rebuilt after the credits edit.\n   - `exit-interview.json`: written by the tool; parses; shape checked.\n   - `PROGRESS.md`: status currently says verify 25/0 and npm test passed, then \"After that run, one text line changed: the credits no longer name the source (plan section 1). Rebuilt; npm run check and browser stages boot, about, standalone rerun. Nothing is left to do.\" Update it with the final verify result.\n   - `PLAN.md`, `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md`: given, unchanged.\n\n   Dev folder `TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601/`:\n   - `labs/game/README.md` (the calls made), `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` (13 friction items, 5 requests, no local patches).\n   - `labs/game/main.ts`, `index.html`.\n   - `scenes/`: settings, components, componentTypes, wobble, seats, flow, ending, days, director, pilot, use, start, tilt, critters, world, island, round, actions, terrain, terrainRound, telegraphs, scoring; `bot/players.ts`; `data/{stations,poses,lures,charts,courses,trays,usables,plaques,days,round,guests}.ts`; `events/{types,kit,index,ring,morning,pose,pond,group,reps,step,line,paddle,garden,plunge,hoop,jog,tilt,tiltWalkers,tiltBot}.ts`; tests `balance.test.ts`, `whole.test.ts`, `audio.test.ts`.\n   - `cast/`: index, clips, builds, roster, `clipdata/borrowed.ts`.\n   - `props/`: kit, core, stations, activities.\n   - `materials/retreat.ts`, `looks/retreat.ts`, `bodies/cast.ts`, `emitters/retreat.ts`, `sounds/{effects,songs}.ts`, `audio/{sound,voice}.ts`, `cameras/shot.ts`.\n   - `hub/`: session.ts, session-client.txt, tags.html, `harness/{harness.html.txt,bridge.js.txt,round.js.txt,README-from-hub.txt}`.\n   - `ui/`: app, frame, appEvents, appInput, names, maps, panel, glyphs, save, shots, nogpu, theme.css, about-data; `hud/{disc,hud,widgets,speech}`; `lines/{index,activities,people,story,plaques}`; `screens/{types,menus,settings,controls,about,programme,results,dev,join,card}`.\n   - `tools/`: `onefile.mjs` (build), `verify.mjs` (one command; `--quick`), `browser.py` (stages: boot keys pad attract pause roam group tenfoot touch about standalone sound mouse credits webkit), `hubcheck.py`, `hubview.py`, `make-replays.mjs`, `shots.py`, `boottime.py`, `exit-interview.mjs`, `borrow-clips.mjs`.\n   - `replays/*.replay.json`: 14 files, goldens recorded for the final sim.\n   - Last source edit, in `labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`: `'Teeter Fit. An original game, inspired by Wii Fit.'` became `'Teeter Fit. An original game.'`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Duplicate ids (`prop:bench`, `sfx:whoosh`, `sfx:kick`): renamed.\n   - `actionMap:front` needed move actions: added.\n   - `spawnProp` placement is `{prop, at, yaw}`: fixed.\n   - Boot far past the hub deadline (engine warms every registered prop part): session spawns no props; dynamic scene import; `gfx.warmUp=asked` in sessions.\n   - Enter on the card too late: the listener moved into the Session constructor; the card shows at once via `showHubCard`.\n   - Seats had actor -1 (setup spawns are queued), so poses never played: `buildIsland` returns ids and `makeSeats(w, ids)` uses them.\n   - Gerald walked off the map (stale intents, helpers overriding): pilot clears intents during events.\n   - Horizon dark band: not outlines or the sea edge; the map goes dark at grazing angles. Fixed with near textured `prop:sea` (360 m), plain `prop:seaFar`, `prop:skirt` haze ring, unlit sea, outline distance fade.\n   - Programme focus restarted the first card: focus on the next item.\n   - Same-frame press opening and closing screens: `openedAt` frame guard.\n   - HUD hint table edit silently failed, causing an `APP_FRAME` crash in Pose Class: fixed; browser tests now assert no engine errors.\n   - Judges removed mid-step crashed `actors` (`PHYSICS_BAD_ARGUMENT`): judges are permanent actors waiting off stage.\n   - Carry-on press leaked into \"use\": `settling` flag keeps front map and modal until confirm is released.\n   - Airborne stance for held people: `Stand` strip. Still Ring now calls `leanSeats`.\n   - Pose Class C perfect bot at 737: pose breath score now uses `inTime()` share of the hold; Lighthouse ring stays 0.14.\n   - Others: `describe()` returns a field list (dev sliders wrote NaN); erasableSyntaxOnly param properties; JSON imports replaced by string constants; pink blobs replaced by Gull and Frog actors with their own bodies; plaster texture brick patches (fallen:0, cracks:0); guest under the pier (fixed body, station y); ambBirds silence; slow frame counted as key repeat; bad tile tones and gull build boot errors; Rapier world per run exhausting memory (shared engine with `seed()`).\n   - Stop-hook pass found \"inspired by Wii Fit\" in the credits: removed and rebuilt.\n   - Running verify from the wrong cwd (`work/`) created stray `work/out`: that folder was looked at and deleted, and the run restarted with an explicit `cd`. A `verify.mjs` process seen in `ps` belonged to another agent and was left alone.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Full game built and verified. The verify run before the credits edit was \"verify: 25 passed, 0 failed\", and `npm test` then had 40 tests passing with exit 0. After the credits edit: `npm run check` ok; browser stages boot, about, standalone 53 passed, 0 failed; only two \"Wii\" occurrences (Source line, `hub:source`); client intact. A full verify plus `npm test` on the final code has just finished in the background; its result is not yet read. The notification's \"exit code 0\" is the wrapper's, not verify's.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Stop hook feedback #1: said the transcript did not show the condition satisfied, questioned the final chat reply and unchecked deliverables, and flagged real-GPU boot and hand-played feel as possibly required.\n   - Stop hook feedback #2: \"The transcript does not show that the required hand-ins were verified against TASK.md's own list, and the transcript never shows TASK.md's deliverables were checked item by item. The last assistant turn says the Source Information and feedback were given 'In my previous message' in the chat, but that message is outside the condition's folder check and is not evidence of a folder deliverable. Its verify run (25 passed) also predates the final credits edit; the browser recheck covered only boot, about and standalone, and the full verify and npm test were not rerun on the final build. The agent also says hand-played feel and real-GPU boot timing were never measured, and the transcript does not show PLAN.md excludes those on this machine. Evidence is insufficient to confirm the condition.\"\n   (Background-task notifications are system events, not user input.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read the final verify and npm test result; fix anything that really fails.\n   - Confirm the deliverable matches the verified build.\n   - Clean up generated `out/` in the dev folder; update `PROGRESS.md`.\n   - Give the final chat reply containing the full Source Information and feedback, an item-by-item hand-in check, and the quotes on hand play and GPU.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Answering stop hook #2. Started in the background from the dev folder: `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs > out/verify.log 2>&1; echo \"verify exit $?\" >> out/verify.log; npm test > out/npmtest.log 2>&1; echo \"npm test exit $?\" >> out/verify.log`. Task b1ech2s0o has completed; `out/verify.log` not yet read.\n\n   Quotes already gathered for the reply:\n   - TASK.md line 50: \"No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\"\n   - TASK.md line 26: \"Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited... Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\"\n   - TASK.md lines 52–57: no physical controller, nobody to listen, no second player, no TV, with stand-ins for each.\n   - PLAN.md lines 146–147: \"Nobody can play by hand here: the delayed-thumb bot (section 16) is how you judge feel.\"\n   - PLAN.md line 631: \"Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\"\n   - PLAN.md line 960: \"Four players stand in for a human, since nobody here can play by hand.\"\n\n   Text for the final reply (matches `about-data.ts` and `exit-interview.json`):\n\n   Source Information:\n   - Date: 2026-11-05 01:56:01\n   - Source: Wii Fit\n   - Plan: PLAN.md\n   - Genre: A 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities round a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual meta game and a comedy story\n   - Perspective: Third person: a chase camera on the island and a purpose-built camera for each activity\n   - Tech: my-3dge at 2dbd829 (full workspace, engine read-only), three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7, TypeScript 5.9; HTML/CSS UI\n   - Art Direction: The engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets: a clean, high-key brochure island\n   - Animation: The engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim, so your thumb is the exercise\n   - Audio: Tracker songs, defineSfx effects, Animalese-style gibberish syllable voices, all code, no audio files, music at 10% by default\n   - Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, up to 4; same-screen Group Class on its own, up to 4 pads\n   - Testing: Headless scripts allowed: bots on 10 seeds per activity, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, browser checks in Playwright, sparing screenshots; no review subagents\n   - Research: The AI Hub protocol README and the my-3dge guide; nothing else was needed beyond the plan\n   - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n   - Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n   - Usage: added on import\n\n   Testing Feedback:\n   - How many issues did testing catch? About 45 across the run, from wrong ids and lint to play-breaking bugs.\n   - How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? Nine: every class pose silently not playing (seats held no actor), a crash at the session scene start, a boot far past the hub deadline, the Programme restarting the first activity for ever, Gerald walking off the map after Island Jog, a press opening and closing the same screen, a frame crash in Pose Class, a crash removing the diving judges in mid-step, and the Carry on press dropping you straight back into the activity.\n   - What was the most helpful test you ran? The scripted playthrough of the whole game with the human-like bot, which proved no softlock on three seeds and found the mid-step crash, and the page drive to the credits with one kind of input, which found the Programme loop and the Carry on bug that the sim could not see.\n   - What was the least helpful test you ran? The look metrics from the shot tool: it told me the pale sky was blown out, and never that a dark band sat on the horizon. A screenshot found that in a second.\n\n   Engine Feedback:\n   - What did you like most about the engine? Play is reproducible and needs no screen. Every activity could be played by bots on ten seeds at step speed, and replays matched in Node and Chromium first time. A pose as one line of numbers, scrubbed from the sim, was a joy.\n   - Did you get stuck or guess wrong? Yes. Spawns inside setup are queued, so looking people up there silently gave every seat no body. I guessed wrong on the prop placement shape, on what describe returns, and on three library ids. The horizon took an hour.\n   - What was the most important thing you had to build yourself? The Wobble Model and the activity framework that makes eleven activities and a finale one shape, with bots; then the whole 10-foot front end: panels, Balance Disc, glyphs, Dev Mode, attract and the hub card.\n   - What was the hardest part about using the engine? Warm-up: the engine builds every registered prop's pipelines when the first prop arrives, which on a software GPU is past the hub's deadline, so a session scene has to draw its pavilion with no props at all.\n   - What did you change in the engine, and why? none\n   - If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be? Warm only the props a scene can spawn.\n\n   Prompt Feedback:\n   - What did you like most about this prompt? The plan marks what was tested and gives real numbers, such as the sway rate that makes a thumb better than doing nothing. Its bots for judging feel were the right answer to nobody being able to play.\n   - What was confusing? The plan was tested on an older engine commit and client hash than I got, so some of its details had moved. Its rule of two short sentences a line sits beside seed lines of five.\n   - What was the hardest thing to do? Judging feel and looks with no person and no real GPU: every sound by numbers, every picture on a software renderer at a few frames a second, and a 45-minute game to hold in one head.\n   - What would you change in this prompt? Pin the engine commit and client version the plan was tested on, and give a boot-time budget for the island as well as the session, since warm-up cost drives how props should be made from the start.\n\n   Honest limits to repeat in the reply:\n   - Nobody played by hand; Hoop Patrol and Island Jog scored 1000 for all three active bots, so they may be easier than the numbers suggest.\n   - All rendering was on a software GPU; the pad was a stub; sound was judged by numbers; mouse lean was tested with synthetic events under pointer lock.\n   - Real-GPU boot is unmeasured. On the software renderer: island about 30 s with `gfx.warmUp=asked`; about 90 s without on a page with props; session about 10 s.\n   - Verify retries memory-killed workers, browsers and the replay stage on this shared machine.\n\n   Deviations already recorded in README: one shot camera; no props in sessions; custom panel widget; Gull and Frog as actors; finale guests walk by their own sums; pose breath score as share in time; only CC0 clips.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Per the last words before this summary: \"Verify and `npm test` are now running from the right folder, on the final code. I'll compare the result with the deliverable when they finish.\"\n   1. Read `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601/out/verify.log`. Expect `verify: N passed, 0 failed`, `verify exit 0`, `npm test exit 0`. Check `out/npmtest.log` for the test counts.\n   2. Run `sha256sum` on `out/verify-game.html` and the root HTML; they should match. If any source changed or a stage really failed, fix it, rebuild the HTML with `node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs ../TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601.html` from the dev folder, regenerate `exit-interview.json` with `node labs/game/tools/exit-interview.mjs ../exit-interview.json`, and re-verify.\n   3. Remove `out/` in the dev folder (not anything of other agents); update `PROGRESS.md` status.\n   4. Send the final chat reply with the verified result, the item-by-item TASK.md check (lines 11, 24, 93, 109), the full Source Information and all three feedback sections, the honest limits, and the TASK.md and PLAN.md quotes showing hand play and real-GPU measurement are not required on this computer.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261105-015601--x54facc-work/9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"24bfc650-771f-48fb-a7a0-9a8b01a66841","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:57:29.489Z","isSynthetic":true}
