{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkNcBDbTjeuoik8HLy89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UWoQ4TbwmoJ9yrU1sX1NCn","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":952},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3413,"cache_read_input_tokens":49797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3413},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"cf81c385-21c4-46f5-9fd3-99339d56d2fa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:58:49.461Z","request_id":"req_011CgkNcAqWrqSM36yGmjFA5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UWoQ4TbwmoJ9yrU1sX1NCn":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","offset":952}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWoQ4TbwmoJ9yrU1sX1NCn","type":"tool_result","content":"952\t## 16. Testing\n953\t\n954\t**One command:** `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` prints only failures and one final count line. `--quick` stops after the Node stages. Rerun it only after changing code it covers. Prefer scripts: screenshots only for what a script cannot check. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n955\t\n956\t**Node stages (seconds to run):**\n957\t\n958\t- `npm run check`.\n959\t- **Model:** the Wobble Model's maths; no input stays in a 0.22 ring only part of the time (about 40%), a held full stick topples, `calm` lowers sway.\n960\t- **Four players stand in for a human, since nobody here can play by hand.** All are bots writing seat input: *perfect* (no delay, gain 3); *human-like* (reads the CoB 250 ms late, gain 1.2, jitter 0.04); *sloppy* (350 ms, gain 0.8, jitter 0.06); *idle* (no input). Delay is a small history buffer in the bot's state. In rhythm and timing activities, the delay and jitter become timing error.\n961\t- **Every activity on 10 seeds:** the four players meet the targets in section 3 (perfect ≥ 750, human-like ≥ 550, sloppy ≥ 300, idle ≤ 500 and below human-like), random input never throws, idle finishes by itself, score within 0–1000, no `NaN`, and activity teardown leaves no stray bodies or entities.\n962\t- **Still Pond:** pressing a fake prompt costs Composure; a no-input run earns exactly the capped result; real breath lifts the score.\n963\t- **Step Class:** hits land in windows at each BPM; misses break the combo.\n964\t- **Morning Check:** age formula bounds; yesterday comparison.\n965\t- **The whole game:** a scripted playthrough with `game.auto`: every day, every activity, the finale's steps, ending at credits, on 3 seeds. It is the softlock finder. Keep it running in Node at step speed.\n966\t- **Reproducibility:** golden replays (one short per activity, one for a whole day) with `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim`; capture and restore continue exactly. Record goldens once content settles (`--update`, with a reason); while tuning, keep few.\n967\t- **Audio data:** every song and syllable renders non-silent (`node x audio`, `node x qa audio`); no audio files in the build.\n968\t\n969\t**Browser stages (the built file, on `file://` where possible).** Use the workspace's `@playwright/test` with `executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH` and flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. Or Python Playwright, already installed. One or two browsers at once; close them. \"Target closed\" means memory: run fewer, don't retry blindly. Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so the game can only run in Chromium; use WebKit only to check the \"no WebGPU\" page.\n970\t\n971\t- **Boot:** `__engine.ready`, zero errors, no WebGPU downgrade errors.\n972\t- **Controller:** replace `navigator.getGamepads` with a stub in an init script (or the engine's `createScriptedGamepad`). Menus work on D-pad and stick, Cross and Circle; glyphs are PlayStation by default; the Settings switch shows Xbox; prompts change to keys the frame a key is pressed, and to mouse on a click.\n973\t- **Keyboard and mouse:** hover moves focus, click picks; keys drive the same flows; pointer-lock lean moves the CoB.\n974\t- **10-foot:** every visible text node at 1920 × 1080 is at least 28 px; no menu over six rows.\n975\t- **Attract:** starts at 10–11 s idle on the title, shows several activities across a loop, exits on a key, a click and a pad press; the save is untouched.\n976\t- **Pause and dev:** pause menu reaches Dev Mode; a slider changes behaviour; Reset restores defaults; jumps work; not present in a session.\n977\t- **Settings:** music 0.1 on a fresh save; volumes persist across reload; Erase asks in-game.\n978\t- **Touch-only:** Playwright's iPhone and tablet profiles in Chromium: \"Controller or keyboard required\", a Settings button that opens by `page.touchscreen.tap`, attract runs, no touch controls in the DOM.\n979\t- **About:** every Source Information field and every feedback answer is on the screen.\n980\t- **Standalone hub checks, as the hub's own test does:** press Enter, Space, Enter, Space; the client is there and inactive; `Math.random` is untouched; the screen is drawn; no errors.\n981\t- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\n982\t- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\n983\t\n984\t**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\n985\t\n986\t---\n987\t\n988\t## 17. Build order\n989\t\n990\tDo the risky integration first. The game should be shippable, in a smaller form, at every milestone.\n991\t\n992\t1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\n993\t2. **The verb.** Wobble Model, action maps, mouse lean, Balance Disc, glyphs, one activity (Still Ring), its bot, tests, dev sliders. Tune until holding still is fun by itself. The bot tells you it is winnable; numbers tell you it isn't trivial.\n994\t3. **The body.** Clip set, scrubbing, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class. Voice system early: it carries the tone.\n995\t4. **The island.** Terrain, sea, look, stations, roam, flow, Programme, Noticeboard, saves, Morning Check, results, Tare.\n996\t5. **The joke.** Still Pond. Then Cairn, plaques, day cycle.\n997\t6. **Water and sand.** The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden.\n998\t7. **The rest.** Step Class, Reps Hall, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog.\n999\t8. **The finale.** Great Tilt, ending, credits.\n1000\t9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\n1001\t10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\n1002\t11. **Polish.** All 200+ lines, songs, ambience, effects, camera moves, rumble, Expert variants, outfits.\n1003\t12. **Finish.** Section 18 and 19.\n1004\t\n1005\t**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\n1006\t\n1007\t---\n1008\t\n1009\t## 18. Done\n1010\t\n1011\t- Every feature in this plan is real: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. `grep -rEi \"todo|fixme|placeholder|stub\" labs/game` is clean (except test words).\n1012\t- A new player can reach the credits from the title with a pad alone, and again with keyboard and mouse alone.\n1013\t- `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` reports zero failures; `npm run check` and `npm test` pass; the engine is unchanged or its patch is declared.\n1014\t- The single HTML is in the place your TASK.md names, opens from `file://`, and fetches nothing.\n1015\t- `labs/game/README.md` says what the game is and the calls you made. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is honest and specific.\n1016\t\n1017\t---\n1018\t\n1019\t## 19. Reports\n1020\t\n1021\tYour TASK.md defines the chat reply, the About / Credits content and the exit interview, in its exact shape. Keep all the answers in one data file (`labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`), so the screen, the reply and the interview agree. They go in the bundle, so write them before the final build, then rerun `verify`.\n1022\t\n1023\t**Keep a running tally as you go** of the issues testing catches, and which were critical: you will be asked for both, and for your most and least helpful test. Note engine surprises in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` when they happen.\n1024\t\n1025\tAnswers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n1026\t\n1027\tHub catalogue suggestions: type `Game`; genre `Sports`; source `Wii Fit`; series empty (the source is its own franchise); players `1–4`; controls \"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both\"; tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `arcade`, `sports`, `story`. Tagline idea: \"Stand still. It is harder than it looks.\"\n1028\t\n1029\t**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\n1030\t\n1031\t---\n1032\t\n1033\t## 20. Brief-to-plan map\n1034\t\n1035\tCheck this before you call it done.\n1036\t\n1037\t| The brief asks for | Where |\n1038\t|---|---|\n1039\t| Genre and perspective chosen to fit | 1, 6 |\n1040\t| Title: playful riff, picked by a real RNG from 50 | Yours, per TASK.md. This plan just says \"the game's title\": on the title screen, hub card, attract banner, About |\n1041\t| Research: your choice | Not needed beyond this plan; report what you did |\n1042\t| Single HTML; downloads optional | 14 (everything inlined) |\n1043\t| Engine's full workspace, engine read-only, own systems on top | 14, 15 |\n1044\t| Art: engine's native style base; new assets for the source's feel | 10 |\n1045\t| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\n1046\t| Audio: all code, no files; gibberish voices; music 10% default | 12 |\n1047\t| Online and multiplayer: hub integration and on its own | 9 |\n1048\t| Dev folder, separate modules, bundle; shared machine rules | 14, 16 |\n1049\t| Performance out of scope | 9 (one protocol deadline only) |\n1050\t| Testing: headless scripts, full playthrough, one command, failures only, sparing screenshots, no review subagents | 16 |\n1051\t| Original game; distinctive world, characters, themes, tone in mechanics, pacing, UX | 1, 2, 3, 13 |\n1052\t| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics; vertical slice; infrastructure to grow | 5, 6, 7, data tables in 5 and 14 |\n1053\t| Dev mode from pause; standard tools; live sliders with reset | 8 |\n1054\t| Attract: 10 s idle, looping, AI may cheat, any input exits | 8 |\n1055\t| Narrative tone like the source | 13 |\n1056\t| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; prompts by last input; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense screens | 4, 8 |\n1057\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, the message, Settings, attract runs | 8 |\n1058\t| Done: no TODOs or stubs | 18 |\n1059\t| Source Information, feedback, About screen, chat reply, exit interview | 8, 19 |\n1060\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dd98077-2f1f-4b79-bf36-2031f176f317","uuid":"bfe55872-dd96-4b56-a8e1-a22f885779eb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:58:49.470Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 16. Testing\n\n**One command:** `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` prints only failures and one final count line. `--quick` stops after the Node stages. Rerun it only after changing code it covers. Prefer scripts: screenshots only for what a script cannot check. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n**Node stages (seconds to run):**\n\n- `npm run check`.\n- **Model:** the Wobble Model's maths; no input stays in a 0.22 ring only part of the time (about 40%), a held full stick topples, `calm` lowers sway.\n- **Four players stand in for a human, since nobody here can play by hand.** All are bots writing seat input: *perfect* (no delay, gain 3); *human-like* (reads the CoB 250 ms late, gain 1.2, jitter 0.04); *sloppy* (350 ms, gain 0.8, jitter 0.06); *idle* (no input). Delay is a small history buffer in the bot's state. In rhythm and timing activities, the delay and jitter become timing error.\n- **Every activity on 10 seeds:** the four players meet the targets in section 3 (perfect ≥ 750, human-like ≥ 550, sloppy ≥ 300, idle ≤ 500 and below human-like), random input never throws, idle finishes by itself, score within 0–1000, no `NaN`, and activity teardown leaves no stray bodies or entities.\n- **Still Pond:** pressing a fake prompt costs Composure; a no-input run earns exactly the capped result; real breath lifts the score.\n- **Step Class:** hits land in windows at each BPM; misses break the combo.\n- **Morning Check:** age formula bounds; yesterday comparison.\n- **The whole game:** a scripted playthrough with `game.auto`: every day, every activity, the finale's steps, ending at credits, on 3 seeds. It is the softlock finder. Keep it running in Node at step speed.\n- **Reproducibility:** golden replays (one short per activity, one for a whole day) with `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim`; capture and restore continue exactly. Record goldens once content settles (`--update`, with a reason); while tuning, keep few.\n- **Audio data:** every song and syllable renders non-silent (`node x audio`, `node x qa audio`); no audio files in the build.\n\n**Browser stages (the built file, on `file://` where possible).** Use the workspace's `@playwright/test` with `executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH` and flags `--no-sandbox --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. Or Python Playwright, already installed. One or two browsers at once; close them. \"Target closed\" means memory: run fewer, don't retry blindly. Firefox and WebKit have no WebGPU here, so the game can only run in Chromium; use WebKit only to check the \"no WebGPU\" page.\n\n- **Boot:** `__engine.ready`, zero errors, no WebGPU downgrade errors.\n- **Controller:** replace `navigator.getGamepads` with a stub in an init script (or the engine's `createScriptedGamepad`). Menus work on D-pad and stick, Cross and Circle; glyphs are PlayStation by default; the Settings switch shows Xbox; prompts change to keys the frame a key is pressed, and to mouse on a click.\n- **Keyboard and mouse:** hover moves focus, click picks; keys drive the same flows; pointer-lock lean moves the CoB.\n- **10-foot:** every visible text node at 1920 × 1080 is at least 28 px; no menu over six rows.\n- **Attract:** starts at 10–11 s idle on the title, shows several activities across a loop, exits on a key, a click and a pad press; the save is untouched.\n- **Pause and dev:** pause menu reaches Dev Mode; a slider changes behaviour; Reset restores defaults; jumps work; not present in a session.\n- **Settings:** music 0.1 on a fresh save; volumes persist across reload; Erase asks in-game.\n- **Touch-only:** Playwright's iPhone and tablet profiles in Chromium: \"Controller or keyboard required\", a Settings button that opens by `page.touchscreen.tap`, attract runs, no touch controls in the DOM.\n- **About:** every Source Information field and every feedback answer is on the screen.\n- **Standalone hub checks, as the hub's own test does:** press Enter, Space, Enter, Space; the client is there and inactive; `Math.random` is untouched; the screen is drawn; no errors.\n- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\n- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\n\n**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Build order\n\nDo the risky integration first. The game should be shippable, in a smaller form, at every milestone.\n\n1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\n2. **The verb.** Wobble Model, action maps, mouse lean, Balance Disc, glyphs, one activity (Still Ring), its bot, tests, dev sliders. Tune until holding still is fun by itself. The bot tells you it is winnable; numbers tell you it isn't trivial.\n3. **The body.** Clip set, scrubbing, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class. Voice system early: it carries the tone.\n4. **The island.** Terrain, sea, look, stations, roam, flow, Programme, Noticeboard, saves, Morning Check, results, Tare.\n5. **The joke.** Still Pond. Then Cairn, plaques, day cycle.\n6. **Water and sand.** The Line, Paddle Glide, Sand Garden.\n7. **The rest.** Step Class, Reps Hall, Hoop Patrol, Cliff Plunge, Island Jog.\n8. **The finale.** Great Tilt, ending, credits.\n9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\n10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\n11. **Polish.** All 200+ lines, songs, ambience, effects, camera moves, rumble, Expert variants, outfits.\n12. **Finish.** Section 18 and 19.\n\n**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Done\n\n- Every feature in this plan is real: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. `grep -rEi \"todo|fixme|placeholder|stub\" labs/game` is clean (except test words).\n- A new player can reach the credits from the title with a pad alone, and again with keyboard and mouse alone.\n- `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` reports zero failures; `npm run check` and `npm test` pass; the engine is unchanged or its patch is declared.\n- The single HTML is in the place your TASK.md names, opens from `file://`, and fetches nothing.\n- `labs/game/README.md` says what the game is and the calls you made. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is honest and specific.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Reports\n\nYour TASK.md defines the chat reply, the About / Credits content and the exit interview, in its exact shape. Keep all the answers in one data file (`labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`), so the screen, the reply and the interview agree. They go in the bundle, so write them before the final build, then rerun `verify`.\n\n**Keep a running tally as you go** of the issues testing catches, and which were critical: you will be asked for both, and for your most and least helpful test. Note engine surprises in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` when they happen.\n\nAnswers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n\nHub catalogue suggestions: type `Game`; genre `Sports`; source `Wii Fit`; series empty (the source is its own franchise); players `1–4`; controls \"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both\"; tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `arcade`, `sports`, `story`. Tagline idea: \"Stand still. It is harder than it looks.\"\n\n**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\n\n---\n\n## 20. Brief-to-plan map\n\nCheck this before you call it done.\n\n| The brief asks for | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit | 1, 6 |\n| Title: playful riff, picked by a real RNG from 50 | Yours, per TASK.md. This plan just says \"the game's title\": on the title screen, hub card, attract banner, About |\n| Research: your choice | Not needed beyond this plan; report what you did |\n| Single HTML; downloads optional | 14 (everything inlined) |\n| Engine's full workspace, engine read-only, own systems on top | 14, 15 |\n| Art: engine's native style base; new assets for the source's feel | 10 |\n| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\n| Audio: all code, no files; gibberish voices; music 10% default | 12 |\n| Online and multiplayer: hub integration and on its own | 9 |\n| Dev folder, separate modules, bundle; shared machine rules | 14, 16 |\n| Performance out of scope | 9 (one protocol deadline only) |\n| Testing: headless scripts, full playthrough, one command, failures only, sparing screenshots, no review subagents | 16 |\n| Original game; distinctive world, characters, themes, tone in mechanics, pacing, UX | 1, 2, 3, 13 |\n| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics; vertical slice; infrastructure to grow | 5, 6, 7, data tables in 5 and 14 |\n| Dev mode from pause; standard tools; live sliders with reset | 8 |\n| Attract: 10 s idle, looping, AI may cheat, any input exits | 8 |\n| Narrative tone like the source | 13 |\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; prompts by last input; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense screens | 4, 8 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, the message, Settings, attract runs | 8 |\n| Done: no TODOs or stubs | 18 |\n| Source Information, feedback, About screen, chat reply, exit interview | 8, 19 |\n","numLines":109,"startLine":952,"totalLines":1060}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UWoQ4TbwmoJ9yrU1sX1NCn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
