{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkQv6CCd2cTwH3JQXBo9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K7BEf7DTa3Bv7V5JNYhr8N","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-015601__x54facc/work/TeeterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-015601; echo \"== yaw convention\"; grep -n \"export function fromCamera\" -A8 engine/sim/*.ts engine/*/camera*.ts 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-120 | head -14; grep -rn \"Math.sin(.*yaw\\|Math.cos(.*yaw\" engine/gfx/cameras/pose.ts | cut -c1-130 | head -6; cat > out/patch5.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nconst edit = (file, pairs) => { let t = readFileSync(file, 'utf8'); for (const [a, b] of pairs) { const n = t.split(a).length - 1; if (n !== 1) throw new Error(`${file}: expected 1 match, got ${n}: ${a.slice(0, 80)}`); t = t.replace(a, () => b); } writeFileSync(file, t); console.log('ok', file, pairs.length); };\n// The sea: back to the plan's one huge prop. The band was never about its size.\nedit('labs/game/props/core.ts', [\n  [\"free('prop:sea', 'The near sea: a flat prop that drifts, so the baked ripples live. Past it the water is plain.', [\\n  box('water', 360, 0.1, 360, 'material:seawater'),\\n]);\", \"free('prop:sea', 'The sea: one huge flat prop that drifts, so the baked ripples live.', [\\n  box('water', 16000, 0.1, 16000, 'material:seawater'),\\n]);\"],\n  [\"free(\\n  'prop:seaFar',\\n  'The far sea: plain colour out to the end of the world. A map at a grazing angle goes dark, so ripples stay near.',\\n  [box('water', 16000, 0.1, 16000, 'material:seaFar')],\\n);\\n\", \"\"],\n]);\nedit('labs/game/scenes/world.ts', [[\"  spawnProp(w, { prop: 'prop:seaFar', at: [0, SEA_Y - 0.06, 0], yaw: 0 });\\n\", \"\"]]);\nedit('labs/game/materials/retreat.ts', [[\"flat('material:seaFar', '#6fd0e8', 1, { unlit: true });\\n\", \"\"]]);\n// The small discs read the camera's real pose.\nedit('labs/game/ui/frame.ts', [\n  [\"  seats: readonly { seat: Seat; wobble: Wobble }[],\\n  camera: unknown,\\n): void {\", \"  seats: readonly { seat: Seat; wobble: Wobble }[],\\n  camera: EngineFrame['camera'],\\n): void {\"],\n  [\"function seatViews(seats: readonly { seat: Seat; wobble: Wobble }[], camera: unknown): SeatView[] | undefined {\", \"function seatViews(seats: readonly { seat: Seat; wobble: Wobble }[], camera: EngineFrame['camera']): SeatView[] | undefined {\"],\n  [\"  const m = (camera as { matrixWorldInverse: { elements: ArrayLike<number> } }).matrixWorldInverse.elements;\\n  const { x, y, z } = STATIONS.pavilion;\\n\", \"  const { x, z } = STATIONS.pavilion;\\n  const [rx, rz] = RIGHT_OF(camera.yaw);\\n\"],\n  [\"    return { seat, wobble, across: m[0] * (x + ox) + m[4] * y + m[8] * (z + oz) + m[12] };\\n\", \"    return { seat, wobble, across: rx * (x + ox - camera.position[0]) + rz * (z + oz - camera.position[2]) };\\n\"],\n]);\n// No overlaps: the prompts stop short of the left foot pill, and Step Class's lane starts past the right one.\nedit('labs/game/ui/theme.css', [\n  [\".tf-prompts {\\n  display: flex;\\n\", \".tf-prompts {\\n  max-width: calc(50vw - 27vh - var(--safe));\\n  display: flex;\\n\"],\n]);\nedit('labs/game/ui/hud/hud.ts', [[\"'Breathe with the guide'\", \"'Breathe in time'\"]]);\n// Honest docs.\nedit('labs/game/README.md', [[\"- **The textured sea is 360 m across, not huge,** with a plain sea beyond it. The pixel look turns off anisotropic filtering, so at a\\n  grazing angle the map falls to its dark far mips, which drew a dark band along the horizon from every low camera.\\n\", \"- **The look's outline has a far larger `depth` threshold than the engine's default, and fades sooner.** The plan's look left it at 0.02,\\n  a share of the distance, which a flat sea crosses at a grazing angle of about 2.3 degrees: a dark band along the horizon from any low camera.\\n\"]]);\nedit('ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md', [[\"5. **A sea.** A huge flat prop as the plan describes shows a dark band along the horizon from any low camera: the pixel look\\n   filters with no anisotropy (`engine/gfx/textures/dataTexture.ts`), so at about 2 degrees of grazing angle the map falls to its\\n   far mips, and those read dark. It also has an edge where it ends. A 360 m textured sea, a plain one beyond it and a haze ring\\n   past the fog end fixed it, after two tries.\", \"5. **Outlines on a big flat prop.** The `outline` filter's `depth` test is a jump as a share of the distance, so any flat prop crosses\\n   its default of 0.02 at a grazing angle of about 2.3 degrees, from any camera height: a huge sea gets a thick dark band along the\\n   horizon. Props are always the `object` part (`engine/gfx/props.ts`), so a sea cannot opt out. I raised `depth` and faded lines sooner,\\n   which also thins ink on far objects, and misdiagnosed it twice first (dark mips, the sea's edge). A slope-aware depth test, or a\\n   prop field for the `environment` part, would fix it. A `water` primitive that fades to the fog and has no edge would save every island.\"]]);\nlet f = readFileSync('ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md', 'utf8');\n// Drop the old closing sentence if it survived on the next line.\nwriteFileSync('ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md', f);\n// The screenshot tool: no recursion when a row is missing.\nedit('labs/game/tools/shots.py', [[\"            pick('__more', 300)\\n        raise RuntimeError(f'no menu row {row}')\\n\", \"            if row == '__more':\\n                break\\n            pick('__more', 300)\\n        raise RuntimeError(f'no menu row {row}')\\n\"]]);\nEOF\nnode out/patch5.mjs; sed -n 22,30p ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | cut -c1-130; sed -n 340,352p labs/game/ui/theme.css | cut -c1-60; grep -n \"tf-lane\" -A10 labs/game/ui/theme.css | sed -n 1,12p | cut -c1-60","description":"Revert the sea, fix camera use, correct the docs","timeout":30000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"sto